1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,402
If it isn't right, I should be clear
even if it's late already.

2
00:00:02,402 --> 00:00:06,173
I've already realized this far too late.

3
00:00:07,407 --> 00:00:10,043
I should just be honest with him,

4
00:00:10,043 --> 00:00:11,744
even if it means I don't choose him,

5
00:00:11,744 --> 00:00:14,614
so Shin Woo can consider someone else
even one day sooner.

6
00:00:14,614 --> 00:00:17,350
That's only fair.

7
00:00:17,350 --> 00:00:19,218
Shin Woo will probably be hurt.

8
00:00:19,218 --> 00:00:23,489
Dragging it out all five days,
then not choosing him would be worse.

9
00:00:23,489 --> 00:00:26,559
I think telling him sooner is right.

10
00:00:26,559 --> 00:00:28,594
He'll be hurt.

11
00:00:28,594 --> 00:00:30,229
Da Hye.

12
00:00:30,229 --> 00:00:31,331
Da Hye.

13
00:00:32,265 --> 00:00:33,700
Da Hye.

14
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:34,567
Who is it?

15
00:00:34,567 --> 00:00:36,169
- Shin Woo.
- Da Hye.

16
00:00:36,169 --> 00:00:37,303
Yes?

17
00:00:37,303 --> 00:00:38,838
- You're back?
- Yes.

18
00:00:38,838 --> 00:00:40,373
It was raining outside.

19
00:00:44,544 --> 00:00:45,645
Did it stop?

20
00:00:47,580 --> 00:00:48,581
It's still drizzling.

21
00:00:48,581 --> 00:00:50,183
Really? This much rain is fine.

22
00:00:50,183 --> 00:00:51,584
No, it's fine. This is nothing.

23
00:00:51,584 --> 00:00:53,119
Do you want to go to the pavilion?

24
00:00:53,519 --> 00:00:59,258
The moment of truth is here.

25
00:00:59,258 --> 00:01:02,295
She said she'd end things with Shin Woo...

26
00:01:02,295 --> 00:01:05,098
or at least that was the implication.

27
00:01:11,671 --> 00:01:14,007
- Look at that pout.
- She looks upset.

28
00:01:14,007 --> 00:01:15,274
She's really pouting.

29
00:01:15,274 --> 00:01:16,909
The mood is tense.

30
00:01:19,178 --> 00:01:20,179
What's on your mind?

31
00:01:25,652 --> 00:01:29,455
There's one thing that worries me most.

32
00:01:31,858 --> 00:01:34,661
I'm more devout than you may realize.

33
00:01:35,728 --> 00:01:37,263
Since faith matters to me,

34
00:01:37,263 --> 00:01:38,965
and you're not religious,

35
00:01:38,965 --> 00:01:40,633
I don't know how this will sound,

36
00:01:40,633 --> 00:01:45,071
but faith is a huge part of my life.

37
00:01:45,071 --> 00:01:46,205
My faith has always shaped...

38
00:01:47,106 --> 00:01:51,411
the future I pictured for myself.

39
00:01:52,311 --> 00:01:54,814
But you've been so warm to me,

40
00:01:54,814 --> 00:01:59,886
and everything you say feels sincere.

41
00:01:59,886 --> 00:02:02,055
So for a moment,
I lost sight of something...

42
00:02:02,055 --> 00:02:05,591
that had always mattered more to me.

43
00:02:05,591 --> 00:02:08,728
I didn't realize I was moving forward
without considering my beliefs.

44
00:02:10,563 --> 00:02:13,032
Then it suddenly hit me earlier.

45
00:02:13,333 --> 00:02:15,435
I hate to say this,

46
00:02:15,435 --> 00:02:17,503
but deep down,

47
00:02:17,503 --> 00:02:20,139
I was relieved...

48
00:02:20,139 --> 00:02:21,507
that Shin Woo wasn't Christian.

49
00:02:21,507 --> 00:02:23,743
Because from where I stand,

50
00:02:23,743 --> 00:02:26,646
this gave her the perfect way out.

51
00:02:26,646 --> 00:02:31,117
She's using religion as her main reason.

52
00:02:32,385 --> 00:02:34,087
First, thank you for telling me.

53
00:02:35,355 --> 00:02:37,690
We've talked about religion...

54
00:02:37,690 --> 00:02:40,426
little by little since our first day.

55
00:02:40,426 --> 00:02:42,795
And many things made me rethink...

56
00:02:42,795 --> 00:02:44,897
my views on religion.

57
00:02:45,465 --> 00:02:46,966
I used to be someone...

58
00:02:46,966 --> 00:02:49,202
who felt uncomfortable...

59
00:02:49,202 --> 00:02:51,170
even going to church with a partner.

60
00:02:51,170 --> 00:02:54,640
But you seemed so pure in word and deed...

61
00:02:54,640 --> 00:02:57,243
that I wanted to go with you.

62
00:02:57,243 --> 00:02:59,345
- That's how I felt.
- "You seemed pure."

63
00:02:59,345 --> 00:03:00,513
See?

64
00:03:02,281 --> 00:03:06,019
Your parents' love helped shape you,

65
00:03:06,019 --> 00:03:07,487
but I also think your faith...

66
00:03:07,487 --> 00:03:11,491
played a huge part in who you became.

67
00:03:12,191 --> 00:03:14,427
Goodness, this is really hard.

68
00:03:14,427 --> 00:03:15,895
This is hard.

69
00:03:16,629 --> 00:03:18,931
You meet someone you like,

70
00:03:18,931 --> 00:03:21,134
but they aren't religious.

71
00:03:21,134 --> 00:03:23,903
Could working through that together...

72
00:03:23,903 --> 00:03:26,572
also be part of the Lord's plan?

73
00:03:27,607 --> 00:03:29,475
He's already a believer.

74
00:03:29,475 --> 00:03:30,877
He's already a believer.

75
00:03:31,310 --> 00:03:33,913
He really knows what to say.

76
00:03:33,913 --> 00:03:36,416
She threw the spear, but he blocked it.

77
00:03:36,416 --> 00:03:39,719
She'd opened an escape route with this,

78
00:03:39,719 --> 00:03:41,788
- and now it's closed.
- Exactly.

79
00:03:41,788 --> 00:03:43,523
It's only been four days...

80
00:03:43,523 --> 00:03:45,758
and he already said "the Lord."

81
00:03:45,758 --> 00:03:46,859
Exactly.

82
00:03:47,660 --> 00:03:50,096
Could this be part of the Lord's plan?

83
00:03:51,097 --> 00:03:52,899
Working through it together?

84
00:03:52,899 --> 00:03:54,267
This just got harder for Da Hye.

85
00:03:57,970 --> 00:03:59,772
Does it have to end?

86
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:02,775
- No, it doesn't.
- Is your mind made up?

87
00:04:02,775 --> 00:04:05,011
I want to work through it, not end it.

88
00:04:06,612 --> 00:04:08,514
I want us to talk and work it out.

89
00:04:09,182 --> 00:04:10,984
I don't want to end this.

90
00:04:13,052 --> 00:04:15,121
Let me pray about it a little longer.

91
00:04:16,556 --> 00:04:17,824
Pray...

92
00:04:17,824 --> 00:04:19,359
a little longer?

93
00:04:19,359 --> 00:04:22,328
She's been checkmated.

94
00:04:22,328 --> 00:04:23,296
What can she do?

95
00:04:23,296 --> 00:04:25,131
She only has one way out now.

96
00:04:25,131 --> 00:04:29,369
"I don't think you're my type. I'm sorry."

97
00:04:29,369 --> 00:04:33,039
Right. Da Hye may simply be too kind...

98
00:04:33,039 --> 00:04:36,576
to say something that might hurt him.

99
00:04:36,576 --> 00:04:39,312
That's how this happened.

100
00:04:39,312 --> 00:04:41,247
She's backed into a corner.

101
00:04:42,315 --> 00:04:43,850
(Ye Chan's mother and Da Hye's mother
are still talking.)

102
00:04:43,850 --> 00:04:45,218
I'll be honest.

103
00:04:45,218 --> 00:04:48,788
Ye Chan says he keeps missing out...

104
00:04:48,788 --> 00:04:52,125
because he never got to talk to her.

105
00:04:52,125 --> 00:04:54,761
Shin Woo came to talk to Ye Chan twice.

106
00:04:54,761 --> 00:04:56,729
He kept asking leading questions.

107
00:04:56,729 --> 00:04:58,598
Ye Chan kept saying
someone was his second or third choice.

108
00:04:58,598 --> 00:05:00,667
Shin Woo suspected Da Hye was among them,

109
00:05:02,268 --> 00:05:03,903
so he kept asking leading questions.

110
00:05:04,370 --> 00:05:06,773
How was it, Ye Chan?

111
00:05:06,773 --> 00:05:09,776
I'm more drawn to one of the three.

112
00:05:10,443 --> 00:05:13,146
- His mother heard it all.
- She did.

113
00:05:13,146 --> 00:05:15,048
If you got a one-on-one dinner,

114
00:05:15,048 --> 00:05:18,117
who would you ask to join you?

115
00:05:18,117 --> 00:05:19,652
Jeong Yoon or Da Hye.

116
00:05:20,019 --> 00:05:21,454
I spoke to Do Yoon last night.

117
00:05:21,921 --> 00:05:26,059
He was very clear about Da Hye.

118
00:05:26,059 --> 00:05:27,827
"I like Da Hye."

119
00:05:27,827 --> 00:05:30,863
"Don't even think about her."

120
00:05:30,863 --> 00:05:32,799
That's basically what he said.

121
00:05:32,799 --> 00:05:36,903
Yesterday, Ye Chan came running down...

122
00:05:36,903 --> 00:05:39,272
to meet Da Hye.

123
00:05:39,272 --> 00:05:41,974
Shin Woo thought he was going to her...

124
00:05:41,974 --> 00:05:43,710
and tried to stop him.

125
00:05:44,777 --> 00:05:45,611
Where are you going?

126
00:05:45,611 --> 00:05:46,679
I'm going down there to talk.

127
00:05:46,679 --> 00:05:48,314
- With whom?
- Da Hye.

128
00:05:48,314 --> 00:05:50,450
Don't go. You can't go.

129
00:05:50,450 --> 00:05:52,885
Sorry, I'm completely drained right now.

130
00:05:53,419 --> 00:05:54,153
Have a good time.

131
00:05:54,153 --> 00:05:55,021
Yes, I'm sorry.

132
00:05:55,021 --> 00:05:56,322
Don't talk to her for too long.

133
00:05:56,589 --> 00:06:00,426
He tried to stop Ye Chan
thinking he was going to see Da Hye.

134
00:06:01,327 --> 00:06:04,430
"Mom, Shin Woo likes her so much."

135
00:06:04,430 --> 00:06:07,767
"I feel guilty liking her too."

136
00:06:07,767 --> 00:06:09,569
It's rare to like someone that much.

137
00:06:09,569 --> 00:06:10,703
Right.

138
00:06:10,703 --> 00:06:13,172
Shin Woo was always very direct.

139
00:06:13,740 --> 00:06:17,076
What disappointed me at the end was...

140
00:06:17,076 --> 00:06:20,413
that with all ten of them together,

141
00:06:20,413 --> 00:06:25,685
he still tried to throw Ye Chan off.

142
00:06:25,685 --> 00:06:29,889
He knew Ye Chan liked Da Hye too,

143
00:06:29,889 --> 00:06:32,258
yet he went there and did that.

144
00:06:32,258 --> 00:06:33,793
That felt cowardly to me.

145
00:06:33,793 --> 00:06:36,262
I was truly disappointed in him.

146
00:06:37,597 --> 00:06:38,598
"Cowardly."

147
00:06:38,598 --> 00:06:39,699
Her mother...

148
00:06:40,166 --> 00:06:42,201
- lost interest.
- She really has.

149
00:06:43,369 --> 00:06:46,339
Shin Woo told Ye Chan all of that.

150
00:06:46,339 --> 00:06:49,742
I hate that Shin Woo treated Ye Chan...

151
00:06:49,742 --> 00:06:51,778
that way.

152
00:06:51,778 --> 00:06:54,881
I hate the idea of manipulating anyone.

153
00:06:56,049 --> 00:06:58,685
One move like that...

154
00:06:58,685 --> 00:07:01,087
makes everything else seem childish.

155
00:07:01,087 --> 00:07:03,189
- She's already over him.
- It seems so.

156
00:07:04,190 --> 00:07:06,025
Once I heard he did that,

157
00:07:06,025 --> 00:07:08,094
it completely changed my mind.

158
00:07:10,730 --> 00:07:13,666
They talk like he committed a crime.

159
00:07:13,666 --> 00:07:15,868
But while they're talking about Ye Chan,

160
00:07:15,868 --> 00:07:17,937
his heart is already somewhere else.

161
00:07:18,604 --> 00:07:20,406
I feel bad for them.

162
00:07:21,574 --> 00:07:22,675
(Jeong Yoon returns to her room.)

163
00:07:22,675 --> 00:07:23,509
Mom, are you asleep?

164
00:07:23,509 --> 00:07:24,911
- Jeong Yoon.
- What is it?

165
00:07:24,911 --> 00:07:27,380
Ye Chan came by to see me.

166
00:07:27,380 --> 00:07:28,948
He came to you instead of me?

167
00:07:28,948 --> 00:07:30,216
He met with you?

168
00:07:30,216 --> 00:07:31,818
You weren't here, so he came to me.

169
00:07:31,818 --> 00:07:34,787
He never got a chance
to have a deep conversation with you.

170
00:07:34,787 --> 00:07:37,657
But he didn't feel it was over yet.

171
00:07:37,657 --> 00:07:38,424
What?

172
00:07:38,424 --> 00:07:39,792
So he said he wanted to talk.

173
00:07:42,028 --> 00:07:43,896
Her mother is putting in a good word.

174
00:07:43,896 --> 00:07:44,630
She is.

175
00:07:44,630 --> 00:07:47,000
"You weren't here, so he came to me."

176
00:07:47,934 --> 00:07:51,637
(Jeong Yoon goes to find Ye Chan.)

177
00:07:51,637 --> 00:07:53,740
Ye Chan, are you in there?

178
00:07:54,307 --> 00:07:55,141
(No one is in Ye Chan's room.)

179
00:07:55,141 --> 00:07:56,109
Where did he go?

180
00:07:56,109 --> 00:07:57,110
He's not here.

181
00:07:58,945 --> 00:08:00,013
This can't be happening.

182
00:08:01,047 --> 00:08:02,181
I'm out of breath.

183
00:08:03,316 --> 00:08:04,784
How does anyone...

184
00:08:04,784 --> 00:08:06,152
get around this place?

185
00:08:07,286 --> 00:08:09,255
(The top-floor resident appears.)

186
00:08:09,255 --> 00:08:10,323
It's raining.

187
00:08:10,323 --> 00:08:11,157
It is.

188
00:08:11,824 --> 00:08:12,859
Who are you, though?

189
00:08:13,960 --> 00:08:14,927
I'm Choi Jeong Yoon.

190
00:08:14,927 --> 00:08:16,829
- I see.
- What do you mean, "Who are you?"

191
00:08:16,829 --> 00:08:19,766
The backlight kept me from seeing you.

192
00:08:19,766 --> 00:08:20,600
When did you get here?

193
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:21,534
Just now.

194
00:08:22,268 --> 00:08:25,405
Thanks for gracing my humble place.

195
00:08:25,405 --> 00:08:27,540
The most popular lady is here.

196
00:08:27,540 --> 00:08:30,076
Mom said you stopped by to talk.

197
00:08:30,076 --> 00:08:31,811
So she told you.

198
00:08:32,912 --> 00:08:35,481
Things didn't go the way I expected.

199
00:08:36,015 --> 00:08:39,952
At first, three of the five women...

200
00:08:39,952 --> 00:08:42,355
caught my interest, and you...

201
00:08:42,355 --> 00:08:44,324
were the one I liked most.

202
00:08:44,324 --> 00:08:46,793
I was naive until yesterday...

203
00:08:47,160 --> 00:08:48,995
and failed to focus more on you.

204
00:08:48,995 --> 00:08:50,263
I think that was my mistake.

205
00:08:50,830 --> 00:08:53,700
Honestly, I liked you a lot.

206
00:08:53,700 --> 00:08:56,269
You were always in my top three.

207
00:08:56,269 --> 00:08:57,337
But then, little by little...

208
00:08:57,337 --> 00:09:00,039
Yes, he slipped down the list.

209
00:09:00,039 --> 00:09:01,174
I think that's what happened...

210
00:09:01,174 --> 00:09:05,445
because others kept giving me reasons.

211
00:09:05,445 --> 00:09:07,680
I started thinking...

212
00:09:07,680 --> 00:09:09,515
you weren't very interested in me.

213
00:09:09,515 --> 00:09:12,218
If you had been, I thought you'd have...

214
00:09:12,218 --> 00:09:14,587
found some way to talk to me once.

215
00:09:15,221 --> 00:09:17,890
And somehow, it took you until now.

216
00:09:17,890 --> 00:09:19,792
This may sound like an excuse,

217
00:09:19,792 --> 00:09:21,527
but I did come by two or three times.

218
00:09:22,228 --> 00:09:25,131
(Ye Chan visited Jeong Yoon last night.)

219
00:09:25,498 --> 00:09:28,368
(He heard In Kwon and Jeong Yoon inside.)

220
00:09:28,368 --> 00:09:29,969
So he did come by.

221
00:09:29,969 --> 00:09:31,471
(He quietly turns around.)

222
00:09:31,771 --> 00:09:36,109
I'm glad Mom told me today.

223
00:09:36,109 --> 00:09:38,111
The religious issue did worry me.

224
00:09:38,111 --> 00:09:40,980
Your mother seemed to prefer...

225
00:09:40,980 --> 00:09:42,482
someone who shared her faith.

226
00:09:42,849 --> 00:09:45,485
Right. When it comes to religion,

227
00:09:45,485 --> 00:09:46,919
I've learned a lot about myself here.

228
00:09:46,919 --> 00:09:49,989
Before I know someone or feel drawn in,

229
00:09:49,989 --> 00:09:52,425
when religion comes up, I realize...

230
00:09:52,425 --> 00:09:55,161
it makes me feel pressured.

231
00:09:55,395 --> 00:09:57,597
I'm not deeply religious.

232
00:09:58,131 --> 00:09:59,832
Ye Chan didn't seem that devout.

233
00:09:59,832 --> 00:10:00,667
That's right.

234
00:10:00,667 --> 00:10:03,302
If religion were his top priority,

235
00:10:03,302 --> 00:10:05,471
he said he'd have met someone at church.

236
00:10:05,471 --> 00:10:06,706
Exactly.

237
00:10:06,706 --> 00:10:09,108
I don't know what tomorrow will bring,

238
00:10:09,108 --> 00:10:10,910
but I'd like to come find you...

239
00:10:10,910 --> 00:10:12,979
and spend more time...

240
00:10:13,279 --> 00:10:16,783
talking with you.

241
00:10:17,617 --> 00:10:20,720
Tomorrow isn't the final choice yet.

242
00:10:21,988 --> 00:10:23,823
For me,

243
00:10:23,823 --> 00:10:26,759
he cleared up...

244
00:10:26,759 --> 00:10:29,362
the concerns I had about faith.

245
00:10:29,362 --> 00:10:32,598
That gave me one less thing to weigh.

246
00:10:33,966 --> 00:10:36,769
(After a confusing night,)

247
00:10:37,804 --> 00:10:41,708
(it's one day before the final choice.)

248
00:10:41,708 --> 00:10:45,345
As of yesterday, I know how I feel.

249
00:10:45,345 --> 00:10:48,281
I'll talk to my first choice now.

250
00:10:48,281 --> 00:10:51,184
Today's my only chance if I find time.

251
00:10:51,184 --> 00:10:52,919
I'll talk to her one last time...

252
00:10:52,919 --> 00:10:54,821
and then the decision...

253
00:10:54,821 --> 00:10:56,990
- is up to Jeong Yoon.
- Right.

254
00:10:56,990 --> 00:10:59,592
Ye Chan seems just like us, though.

255
00:11:00,760 --> 00:11:02,895
We didn't talk about that yesterday.

256
00:11:02,895 --> 00:11:05,965
I heard Ye Chan spoke with her last night.

257
00:11:05,965 --> 00:11:08,134
I don't want to fight them, but...

258
00:11:09,168 --> 00:11:10,770
Choi Jeong Yoon is...

259
00:11:10,770 --> 00:11:13,806
- the most popular.
- She certainly is.

260
00:11:13,806 --> 00:11:15,208
She's winning by a landslide.

261
00:11:16,209 --> 00:11:17,443
There's no reason not to try...

262
00:11:17,443 --> 00:11:19,912
to win her over.

263
00:11:19,912 --> 00:11:21,881
I should show her I'm serious.

264
00:11:21,881 --> 00:11:23,116
- Right.
- Absolutely.

265
00:11:23,583 --> 00:11:24,450
(Knock, knock)

266
00:11:24,450 --> 00:11:25,284
Yes?

267
00:11:27,820 --> 00:11:29,689
(In Kwon visits Jeong Yoon's room.)

268
00:11:29,689 --> 00:11:31,357
- You startled me.
- Good morning.

269
00:11:31,357 --> 00:11:32,925
What's that?

270
00:11:32,925 --> 00:11:33,760
Coffee.

271
00:11:33,760 --> 00:11:35,328
(Two coffees,
including one for her mother)

272
00:11:35,328 --> 00:11:37,630
Morning coffee.

273
00:11:37,630 --> 00:11:41,200
In Kwon has finally
gotten his act together.

274
00:11:42,869 --> 00:11:44,837
- Thank you.
- How'd he know you drink it iced?

275
00:11:45,938 --> 00:11:47,006
Thanks. I'll enjoy it.

276
00:11:47,006 --> 00:11:48,207
I didn't know she was so popular.

277
00:11:49,342 --> 00:11:50,743
What did he say?

278
00:11:50,743 --> 00:11:51,911
"It looked like she'd be busy."

279
00:11:51,911 --> 00:11:54,213
"I didn't know she was this popular."

280
00:11:55,081 --> 00:11:56,616
He even wrote a note.

281
00:11:57,083 --> 00:11:59,285
(You'll be busy today. Stay focused.)

282
00:11:59,285 --> 00:12:00,753
That's a good line.

283
00:12:01,354 --> 00:12:03,156
(From Ondal)

284
00:12:03,156 --> 00:12:04,724
In the note...

285
00:12:04,724 --> 00:12:08,461
Her mother mentioned the story
of "Princess Pyeonggang and Ondal."

286
00:12:08,995 --> 00:12:11,764
I asked if she was Princess Pyeonggang.

287
00:12:11,764 --> 00:12:15,668
She wanted to make someone General Ondal.

288
00:12:15,668 --> 00:12:19,138
I remembered discussing it with them,

289
00:12:19,138 --> 00:12:22,875
so I signed it "Ondal."

290
00:12:23,609 --> 00:12:24,944
(Laughing)

291
00:12:24,944 --> 00:12:25,778
She loves it.

292
00:12:25,778 --> 00:12:28,047
My gosh.

293
00:12:28,748 --> 00:12:30,516
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

294
00:12:30,516 --> 00:12:32,418
Jeong Yoon, can we talk for a minute?

295
00:12:32,418 --> 00:12:34,520
Yes, just a minute.

296
00:12:34,520 --> 00:12:36,055
She's busy.

297
00:12:36,055 --> 00:12:37,190
Goodness.

298
00:12:38,691 --> 00:12:40,660
There you are. It's cold.

299
00:12:40,660 --> 00:12:41,894
I thought you'd moved out.

300
00:12:42,996 --> 00:12:43,863
What are you talking about?

301
00:12:43,863 --> 00:12:44,964
This happens every time I come.

302
00:12:45,732 --> 00:12:47,200
Do you want to go over there?

303
00:12:47,200 --> 00:12:48,301
I was talking with someone else.

304
00:12:48,534 --> 00:12:50,470
When I came back yesterday,

305
00:12:50,470 --> 00:12:53,139
Mom said you'd stopped by,
but it was too late.

306
00:12:53,139 --> 00:12:55,108
She must be thinking, "He's back again."

307
00:12:55,108 --> 00:12:55,842
That's not true.

308
00:12:56,976 --> 00:12:57,810
(Seong Mo visited her room last night.)

309
00:12:57,810 --> 00:12:58,778
Jeong Yoon.

310
00:13:00,013 --> 00:13:00,880
Are you in there?

311
00:13:00,880 --> 00:13:03,082
- Come in.
- I came to talk to Jeong Yoon.

312
00:13:03,082 --> 00:13:04,584
Jeong Yoon isn't here.

313
00:13:04,584 --> 00:13:05,985
She isn't? Where did she go?

314
00:13:05,985 --> 00:13:08,187
They kept missing each other.

315
00:13:08,721 --> 00:13:11,190
(He waits outside Jeong Yoon's room.)

316
00:13:11,958 --> 00:13:12,792
(Flops down)

317
00:13:12,792 --> 00:13:16,029
He has an athlete's determination.

318
00:13:17,163 --> 00:13:20,366
I never saw you yesterday.

319
00:13:21,167 --> 00:13:22,902
Our timing was always off.

320
00:13:22,902 --> 00:13:23,936
Then I started wondering...

321
00:13:24,404 --> 00:13:27,774
if I wasn't making chances happen.

322
00:13:27,774 --> 00:13:29,609
Should I be more proactive?

323
00:13:30,576 --> 00:13:33,546
I didn't want any regrets today.

324
00:13:33,546 --> 00:13:35,048
So you made your own chance.

325
00:13:35,048 --> 00:13:36,315
Exactly. That's why I'm here.

326
00:13:37,717 --> 00:13:40,353
I rushed through breakfast to get here.

327
00:13:46,326 --> 00:13:49,862
Today, you may choose your own dates.

328
00:13:49,862 --> 00:13:50,663
What?

329
00:13:51,964 --> 00:13:55,735
Ask anyone you like out on a date.

330
00:13:58,471 --> 00:13:59,472
Perfect timing.

331
00:14:01,040 --> 00:14:03,343
In Kwon had you to himself yesterday,

332
00:14:03,343 --> 00:14:05,578
so I want you all to myself today.

333
00:14:05,578 --> 00:14:06,312
Is that so?

334
00:14:06,312 --> 00:14:07,613
- You won't run away, right?
- I won't.

335
00:14:07,613 --> 00:14:08,348
This feels a little...

336
00:14:08,348 --> 00:14:09,882
No.

337
00:14:10,450 --> 00:14:12,452
We're running out of time.

338
00:14:12,452 --> 00:14:13,886
Can you get ready in five minutes?

339
00:14:14,988 --> 00:14:15,888
(Ye Chan jumps up at the open-date alert.)

340
00:14:15,888 --> 00:14:16,723
Look at him.

341
00:14:18,324 --> 00:14:19,525
Goodness.

342
00:14:19,525 --> 00:14:20,994
(Scrunches down)

343
00:14:21,861 --> 00:14:24,097
(Scrunches down again)

344
00:14:25,264 --> 00:14:28,067
I was already talking to Jeong Yoon.

345
00:14:28,067 --> 00:14:29,869
And right then...

346
00:14:29,869 --> 00:14:31,237
- The alert went off?
- Yes.

347
00:14:31,237 --> 00:14:32,538
How long are you going to talk?

348
00:14:32,538 --> 00:14:34,707
- We'll go outside.
- Outside?

349
00:14:34,707 --> 00:14:35,742
(In Kwon and Seong Mo want the same date.)

350
00:14:35,742 --> 00:14:36,709
What do they do?

351
00:14:36,709 --> 00:14:37,844
Since you both chose her...

352
00:14:37,844 --> 00:14:39,645
- Ye Chan may come too.
- Right.

353
00:14:39,946 --> 00:14:41,781
Should we each take a time slot?

354
00:14:41,781 --> 00:14:43,383
I kept her too long yesterday.

355
00:14:43,383 --> 00:14:44,517
What time should each of you come by?

356
00:14:44,517 --> 00:14:45,918
The three of you can work it out.

357
00:14:45,918 --> 00:14:47,887
(Jeong Yoon is unaware of the rotation.)

358
00:14:47,887 --> 00:14:50,189
In Kwon, Ye Chan, and Seong Mo.
She's busy today.

359
00:14:50,189 --> 00:14:52,558
Jeong Yoon must be loving this.

360
00:14:53,993 --> 00:14:57,597
(Do Yoon goes to find someone.)

361
00:15:00,600 --> 00:15:02,669
Can we talk for a minute?

362
00:15:02,669 --> 00:15:05,705
(Do Yoon asks In Kwon to talk.)

363
00:15:06,005 --> 00:15:07,206
I was really surprised.

364
00:15:08,041 --> 00:15:11,377
I'd already sorted out my feelings.

365
00:15:11,744 --> 00:15:13,646
So talking with the others...

366
00:15:13,646 --> 00:15:15,348
felt more platonic.

367
00:15:15,615 --> 00:15:17,350
Have you eaten?

368
00:15:17,350 --> 00:15:19,352
Just a little. The curry wasn't very good.

369
00:15:19,352 --> 00:15:20,687
Then do you want to get something to eat?

370
00:15:20,687 --> 00:15:21,888
Let's go eat.

371
00:15:23,856 --> 00:15:24,824
What works for you?

372
00:15:24,824 --> 00:15:25,792
Let's eat out.

373
00:15:26,292 --> 00:15:28,361
It looks like Do Yoon...

374
00:15:28,361 --> 00:15:31,898
knows how she feels now.

375
00:15:31,898 --> 00:15:35,968
But the other person seems
to have made up his mind too.

376
00:15:37,403 --> 00:15:38,571
(Ye Chan finally heads out.)

377
00:15:38,571 --> 00:15:40,773
It's a long way down from the top.

378
00:15:42,342 --> 00:15:43,176
Good morning.

379
00:15:44,277 --> 00:15:47,680
I already spoke to Jeong Yoon.

380
00:15:48,281 --> 00:15:50,616
I'll go now and come back later.

381
00:15:50,616 --> 00:15:51,684
Then we'll rotate.

382
00:15:51,684 --> 00:15:52,785
(He offers Ye Chan a rotation date.)

383
00:15:52,785 --> 00:15:54,454
That's what we've planned.

384
00:15:54,454 --> 00:15:55,722
Split the time?

385
00:15:56,456 --> 00:15:57,523
Is anyone there?

386
00:15:57,523 --> 00:15:59,125
(He goes tell Jeong Yoon the news.)

387
00:15:59,125 --> 00:16:01,227
We heard we could choose our own dates.

388
00:16:01,227 --> 00:16:02,929
If several people choose one person,

389
00:16:02,929 --> 00:16:05,631
we thought time slots would work better
than going on a date altogether.

390
00:16:06,866 --> 00:16:08,634
- In Kwon will come too.
- Is that so?

391
00:16:08,634 --> 00:16:11,070
So the three of us will take turns.

392
00:16:11,070 --> 00:16:12,572
How about 90 minutes each?

393
00:16:12,572 --> 00:16:14,073
Including travel time.

394
00:16:14,073 --> 00:16:15,508
That's very practical.

395
00:16:15,508 --> 00:16:17,510
So around noon or 12:30 p.m.?

396
00:16:17,510 --> 00:16:18,544
12:30 p.m.?

397
00:16:18,544 --> 00:16:19,379
All right.

398
00:16:19,379 --> 00:16:20,513
See you later.

399
00:16:20,780 --> 00:16:23,383
(He leaves after dividing up the time.)

400
00:16:24,951 --> 00:16:28,554
(Shin Woo is also heading somewhere.)

401
00:16:28,755 --> 00:16:30,223
This is...

402
00:16:31,724 --> 00:16:34,260
- Da Hye.
- Da Hye.

403
00:16:34,460 --> 00:16:35,928
- No.
- What do we do?

404
00:16:35,928 --> 00:16:38,097
He should've taken at least one break.

405
00:16:38,097 --> 00:16:40,366
He goes right back to calling her name.

406
00:16:40,366 --> 00:16:42,402
Our ever-devoted Shin Woo.

407
00:16:43,336 --> 00:16:44,237
Da Hye.

408
00:16:45,238 --> 00:16:46,172
Da Hye.

409
00:16:47,140 --> 00:16:48,274
Yes?

410
00:16:48,274 --> 00:16:50,043
- Can you come out now?
- Yes.

411
00:16:50,043 --> 00:16:51,210
Do you want to go on a date with me?

412
00:16:57,550 --> 00:16:59,752
- I'll be back in two hours.
- What a shame.

413
00:17:00,553 --> 00:17:04,490
Da Hye shouldn't go
on a two-hour date with him.

414
00:17:04,490 --> 00:17:07,894
She should've gone to see Ye Chan.

415
00:17:07,894 --> 00:17:10,396
Why didn't she?

416
00:17:10,396 --> 00:17:13,466
Da Hye is being very passive too.

417
00:17:13,466 --> 00:17:15,535
Maybe she thought he'd come to her.

418
00:17:15,535 --> 00:17:18,004
But she waited, and he didn't.

419
00:17:19,205 --> 00:17:21,641
(Da Hye and Shin Woo leave for a date.)

420
00:17:21,641 --> 00:17:25,111
There's something I want to say.

421
00:17:25,111 --> 00:17:28,981
I found a good solution
to what worried us yesterday.

422
00:17:28,981 --> 00:17:32,418
I slept on it and even dreamed about it.

423
00:17:32,418 --> 00:17:34,487
Let's talk about that again
in the evening.

424
00:17:34,487 --> 00:17:36,689
Talking now may ruin my appetite.

425
00:17:36,689 --> 00:17:38,691
Then make time for me tonight.

426
00:17:38,691 --> 00:17:39,892
All right.

427
00:17:40,360 --> 00:17:42,996
(The air suddenly turns cold.)

428
00:17:42,996 --> 00:17:45,665
We had more to discuss from yesterday,

429
00:17:45,665 --> 00:17:49,102
so I thought we needed to keep talking.

430
00:17:49,102 --> 00:17:52,205
But it felt a little too soon,

431
00:17:52,205 --> 00:17:54,807
so I decided to take a breather.

432
00:17:57,377 --> 00:17:59,812
It's the Korean Culture Theme Park.

433
00:17:59,812 --> 00:18:03,149
(A unique date to lighten the mood)

434
00:18:03,616 --> 00:18:05,852
Good call wearing something comfortable.

435
00:18:05,852 --> 00:18:07,687
Korean Culture Theme Park.

436
00:18:08,921 --> 00:18:10,423
- This is great.
- It is.

437
00:18:11,057 --> 00:18:12,125
Archery Experience.

438
00:18:12,759 --> 00:18:13,893
I'll shoot it far.

439
00:18:16,095 --> 00:18:17,030
(Shin Woo misses.)

440
00:18:17,030 --> 00:18:17,797
(Da Hye hits the target.)

441
00:18:18,865 --> 00:18:19,932
That's scary.

442
00:18:19,932 --> 00:18:20,867
I'm good, right?

443
00:18:21,501 --> 00:18:23,469
(Shin Woo tries again.)

444
00:18:24,137 --> 00:18:26,305
(He hits Da Hye's target.)

445
00:18:26,539 --> 00:18:28,174
Da Hye, you know
that's how I feel for you, right?

446
00:18:29,075 --> 00:18:31,010
Shoot at yours, not mine.

447
00:18:31,678 --> 00:18:33,546
I should get farther away.

448
00:18:33,746 --> 00:18:35,782
- "Aim at your own."
- Exactly.

449
00:18:35,782 --> 00:18:37,283
Isn't this already over?

450
00:18:37,283 --> 00:18:39,786
At this point, it practically is.

451
00:18:40,186 --> 00:18:42,121
(Shakes his head)

452
00:18:42,121 --> 00:18:43,556
Can I tell you calmly?

453
00:18:43,556 --> 00:18:45,191
Yes.

454
00:18:45,191 --> 00:18:47,193
I want to explain this at length,

455
00:18:47,193 --> 00:18:48,361
but to give you the short version,

456
00:18:48,361 --> 00:18:49,962
I'll try to find faith.

457
00:18:49,962 --> 00:18:52,332
But only if effort can get me there.

458
00:18:52,332 --> 00:18:54,901
I don't know if it can.

459
00:18:55,768 --> 00:18:58,137
Honestly, I'd prefer...

460
00:18:58,137 --> 00:19:01,641
for us to share the same values.

461
00:19:01,641 --> 00:19:03,309
What I really want...

462
00:19:03,309 --> 00:19:06,346
is someone certain about their faith.

463
00:19:06,346 --> 00:19:08,414
When your father asked that question...

464
00:19:09,148 --> 00:19:13,586
If two people's faiths...

465
00:19:13,586 --> 00:19:15,888
don't align,

466
00:19:15,888 --> 00:19:17,890
it's best to end things quickly.

467
00:19:19,892 --> 00:19:23,329
Because of that,

468
00:19:23,329 --> 00:19:27,467
I feel even more pressure...

469
00:19:27,467 --> 00:19:29,869
about what happens if things go wrong.

470
00:19:29,869 --> 00:19:34,107
My parents have made it clear
they won't pressure me over religion.

471
00:19:34,107 --> 00:19:35,274
And they mean it.

472
00:19:35,274 --> 00:19:36,542
You don't need to feel any pressure.

473
00:19:36,542 --> 00:19:38,378
Thank you for saying that.

474
00:19:38,378 --> 00:19:39,645
Like I said before,

475
00:19:39,645 --> 00:19:42,348
I never want to pressure you, Da Hye.

476
00:19:42,348 --> 00:19:43,516
If...

477
00:19:43,516 --> 00:19:44,784
I'm already feeling pressured.

478
00:19:44,784 --> 00:19:45,985
No.

479
00:19:45,985 --> 00:19:48,054
You already feel...

480
00:19:48,054 --> 00:19:49,522
There's no need to feel pressured.

481
00:19:49,522 --> 00:19:51,824
Even if you aren't pressuring me...

482
00:19:51,824 --> 00:19:52,792
You still feel it?

483
00:19:52,792 --> 00:19:55,395
It's coming from my own feelings.

484
00:19:55,395 --> 00:19:57,363
- So yes, I feel pressured.
- Really?

485
00:19:57,363 --> 00:19:58,798
And here's why.

486
00:19:58,798 --> 00:20:01,267
Your mother cried
as soon as she came in yesterday.

487
00:20:01,668 --> 00:20:03,569
Why are you crying, ma'am?

488
00:20:03,569 --> 00:20:07,407
(His mother burst into tears on the date.)

489
00:20:07,674 --> 00:20:08,975
I kept thinking about that feeling.

490
00:20:08,975 --> 00:20:10,410
I thought of it 500 and 5,000 times,
even 50,000 times.

491
00:20:10,410 --> 00:20:12,879
It was the feeling I'd imagined.

492
00:20:12,879 --> 00:20:14,547
I realized your mother felt it too.

493
00:20:14,547 --> 00:20:16,282
It felt like confirmation.

494
00:20:16,282 --> 00:20:18,151
Remember when you introduced yourself?

495
00:20:18,151 --> 00:20:19,986
You said,
"There's only one person I like."

496
00:20:19,986 --> 00:20:23,189
She must've felt frustrated right then.

497
00:20:23,189 --> 00:20:25,158
She wasn't frustrated at all.

498
00:20:25,158 --> 00:20:26,492
That's a misunderstanding.

499
00:20:26,492 --> 00:20:27,527
My mother said...

500
00:20:27,527 --> 00:20:30,096
she was so grateful she cried,
and they were tears of gratitude.

501
00:20:31,230 --> 00:20:32,565
She truly meant it.

502
00:20:32,565 --> 00:20:34,033
Your mother had her reasons too.

503
00:20:34,033 --> 00:20:35,201
What my mom said is...

504
00:20:35,201 --> 00:20:37,170
No, don't. Please tell me later.

505
00:20:37,170 --> 00:20:38,404
Goodness.

506
00:20:39,339 --> 00:20:40,707
At this point...

507
00:20:40,707 --> 00:20:42,642
Please don't.

508
00:20:42,642 --> 00:20:43,810
Please.

509
00:20:45,044 --> 00:20:46,813
I was a little flustered.

510
00:20:46,813 --> 00:20:49,849
Da Hye still seemed to have...

511
00:20:49,849 --> 00:20:53,353
some unresolved feelings about us.

512
00:20:54,854 --> 00:20:59,359
I think Da Hye has lost interest now.

513
00:20:59,359 --> 00:21:01,561
But Shin Woo still...

514
00:21:01,561 --> 00:21:03,930
doesn't seem to realize it.

515
00:21:03,930 --> 00:21:09,535
He thinks religion is the only issue,

516
00:21:09,535 --> 00:21:12,038
so he keeps trying to talk it through.

517
00:21:12,038 --> 00:21:14,807
Da Hye needs to be clear with him now...

518
00:21:14,807 --> 00:21:17,543
and decide what she wants.

519
00:21:18,011 --> 00:21:19,278
(Ha Yoon and Dong Young's date)

520
00:21:19,278 --> 00:21:20,713
Your mother must be worried...

521
00:21:20,713 --> 00:21:22,548
about the long distance, right?

522
00:21:24,117 --> 00:21:27,153
Yes, because she wants me...

523
00:21:27,153 --> 00:21:30,289
to date someone she can see me marrying.

524
00:21:34,494 --> 00:21:35,595
That's what she wants.

525
00:21:36,596 --> 00:21:40,066
(Her mother's words bring sudden silence.)

526
00:21:40,466 --> 00:21:42,402
You only recently opened your clinic.

527
00:21:42,402 --> 00:21:43,903
Isn't it a little overwhelming?

528
00:21:44,470 --> 00:21:45,605
It's fun,

529
00:21:45,605 --> 00:21:46,906
but when you run a business,

530
00:21:47,974 --> 00:21:49,075
after you leave work...

531
00:21:49,075 --> 00:21:51,844
- There's more work?
- It's a different task.

532
00:21:51,844 --> 00:21:55,348
My set schedule is only four days a week.

533
00:21:55,348 --> 00:21:56,516
At first,

534
00:21:56,516 --> 00:21:58,618
there's just too much work.

535
00:21:59,018 --> 00:22:01,587
I could easily move to Seoul.

536
00:22:03,156 --> 00:22:05,191
That was quite a buildup.
It was long, wasn't it?

537
00:22:05,191 --> 00:22:06,292
It was.

538
00:22:08,928 --> 00:22:10,063
Well...

539
00:22:10,063 --> 00:22:12,031
But the mood...

540
00:22:13,833 --> 00:22:17,270
Ha Yoon's mood seems...

541
00:22:17,270 --> 00:22:19,605
- Different.
- Doesn't it?

542
00:22:20,239 --> 00:22:22,141
Until three days ago,

543
00:22:22,141 --> 00:22:24,610
the whole world felt gloomy and bleak.

544
00:22:24,610 --> 00:22:26,312
But starting two days ago,

545
00:22:26,312 --> 00:22:28,981
the world began to look brighter...

546
00:22:28,981 --> 00:22:31,017
because of you.

547
00:22:33,152 --> 00:22:35,621
Since then, you've brightened my world.

548
00:22:39,525 --> 00:22:40,493
But you know,

549
00:22:40,493 --> 00:22:42,662
you're much more sentimental than I am.

550
00:22:42,662 --> 00:22:43,629
I'm a Thinking Type, though.

551
00:22:44,731 --> 00:22:47,700
I've never heard anyone say,
"The world brightened."

552
00:22:50,436 --> 00:22:51,404
Your world got brighter.

553
00:22:53,706 --> 00:22:55,441
How is your world, Ha Yoon?

554
00:22:55,441 --> 00:22:56,376
My world?

555
00:22:56,743 --> 00:22:58,244
What is my world like?

556
00:23:00,046 --> 00:23:01,080
Well...

557
00:23:02,648 --> 00:23:05,385
With the long-distance issue unresolved,

558
00:23:05,385 --> 00:23:08,521
I wanted to see if my feelings...

559
00:23:08,521 --> 00:23:11,624
would grow strong enough to overcome it.

560
00:23:11,624 --> 00:23:14,060
But I think Dong Young
understood my choice...

561
00:23:14,060 --> 00:23:15,028
as "Let's date."

562
00:23:16,429 --> 00:23:19,298
That's how he interpreted it.

563
00:23:19,298 --> 00:23:21,534
So being around someone that excited...

564
00:23:21,534 --> 00:23:23,236
made me...

565
00:23:23,236 --> 00:23:25,772
pull back a little.

566
00:23:26,172 --> 00:23:28,574
Realistically, this is tough.

567
00:23:28,574 --> 00:23:32,545
Her mom is upset about the distance,

568
00:23:32,545 --> 00:23:34,814
but he says she brightened his world.

569
00:23:35,248 --> 00:23:38,918
So Yang Ha Yoon came to her senses.

570
00:23:39,686 --> 00:23:41,621
Someone moving to Seoul alone...

571
00:23:41,621 --> 00:23:45,458
just to be with you...

572
00:23:45,458 --> 00:23:47,593
- could feel like a huge burden.
- It could.

573
00:23:47,593 --> 00:23:49,028
But she wanted him to come.

574
00:23:49,028 --> 00:23:51,164
She wanted that.

575
00:23:51,164 --> 00:23:52,899
My world just got darker.

576
00:23:54,400 --> 00:23:56,936
Finally, we got a one-on-one date outside.

577
00:23:58,471 --> 00:24:00,740
(Seong Mo and Jeong Yoon's date)

578
00:24:00,740 --> 00:24:02,809
Our workplaces are close by.

579
00:24:02,809 --> 00:24:04,744
- I can visit, right?
- Yes.

580
00:24:04,744 --> 00:24:05,611
I was planning to visit.

581
00:24:05,611 --> 00:24:07,580
I thought I could drop by sometime too.

582
00:24:07,580 --> 00:24:10,249
We could eat if our schedules line up.

583
00:24:10,550 --> 00:24:13,086
Honestly, the first thing...

584
00:24:13,086 --> 00:24:14,821
that really drew me to you...

585
00:24:14,821 --> 00:24:16,556
was how close you live.

586
00:24:16,556 --> 00:24:18,691
You're incredibly close by.

587
00:24:18,691 --> 00:24:21,227
- That's my top priority.
- Mine too.

588
00:24:21,227 --> 00:24:22,996
I'm working in Hakdong too.

589
00:24:22,996 --> 00:24:24,697
So when you said "Hakdong,"
I couldn't believe it.

590
00:24:24,697 --> 00:24:26,632
I wanted to know exactly where.

591
00:24:26,899 --> 00:24:30,303
Don't you have questions for me?

592
00:24:30,303 --> 00:24:31,604
- Questions?
- None?

593
00:24:32,372 --> 00:24:35,208
I know your personality better now.

594
00:24:35,775 --> 00:24:37,243
Can you see me more clearly now?

595
00:24:37,243 --> 00:24:40,947
I wrote down your strengths...

596
00:24:40,947 --> 00:24:42,582
and why I like you.

597
00:24:42,582 --> 00:24:43,983
I overthought it, so I wrote it all down.

598
00:24:43,983 --> 00:24:45,885
Really? You wrote that down?

599
00:24:45,885 --> 00:24:47,553
How many did you write? A lot?

600
00:24:47,553 --> 00:24:49,355
- A fair number.
- Really?

601
00:24:49,355 --> 00:24:50,456
That's kind of cute.

602
00:24:50,456 --> 00:24:52,425
I even wrote
that you can hold your liquor.

603
00:24:52,425 --> 00:24:54,027
- That too?
- Every little detail.

604
00:24:55,261 --> 00:24:56,896
A supportive woman.

605
00:24:56,896 --> 00:24:59,332
Someone really wrote all that down.

606
00:24:59,332 --> 00:25:01,234
- Likes sushi.
- Likes sushi.

607
00:25:03,002 --> 00:25:06,506
(He filled a page while thinking of her.)

608
00:25:06,506 --> 00:25:09,108
I just get the sense...

609
00:25:09,108 --> 00:25:10,610
you're very well-rounded.

610
00:25:10,610 --> 00:25:14,414
Nothing feels lacking or overdone.

611
00:25:15,982 --> 00:25:17,417
So make a wise choice.

612
00:25:17,417 --> 00:25:19,519
You're supposed to ask me questions.

613
00:25:20,186 --> 00:25:23,890
She does look the most comfortable...

614
00:25:23,890 --> 00:25:27,460
more than with Ye Chan or In Kwon.

615
00:25:28,061 --> 00:25:30,730
Have you made up your mind now,

616
00:25:30,730 --> 00:25:32,298
about how interested you are?

617
00:25:32,298 --> 00:25:34,167
Yes, I have.

618
00:25:34,167 --> 00:25:35,234
You have?

619
00:25:37,804 --> 00:25:40,173
Yes. Now that I've decided,

620
00:25:40,173 --> 00:25:41,574
I can go to my room and sleep.

621
00:25:41,574 --> 00:25:42,575
Is that so?

622
00:25:44,477 --> 00:25:45,745
Living nearby...

623
00:25:45,745 --> 00:25:48,815
matters a great deal to me,

624
00:25:48,815 --> 00:25:51,417
so that made me more interested in him.

625
00:25:51,417 --> 00:25:54,687
I felt much more at ease than
when we talked shortly in the lodging,

626
00:25:54,687 --> 00:25:58,091
and I liked that he made me laugh.

627
00:25:58,591 --> 00:26:00,026
It's fun being out with you.

628
00:26:00,026 --> 00:26:01,794
- It feels completely different.
- Really?

629
00:26:01,794 --> 00:26:03,196
Yes. Don't you think so?

630
00:26:03,196 --> 00:26:04,564
I do.

631
00:26:04,564 --> 00:26:06,833
Everyone always tells me...

632
00:26:06,833 --> 00:26:09,369
that once I meet someone I truly love,

633
00:26:09,369 --> 00:26:11,871
I'll probably get married right away.

634
00:26:11,871 --> 00:26:13,773
They think I'll become a different person.

635
00:26:13,773 --> 00:26:16,743
I do have an age in mind, though.

636
00:26:16,743 --> 00:26:18,277
About 33.

637
00:26:18,277 --> 00:26:19,345
Thirty-three?

638
00:26:19,345 --> 00:26:20,580
That's two years away.

639
00:26:20,580 --> 00:26:22,281
Yes, because I'm a woman and...

640
00:26:22,281 --> 00:26:25,151
But waiting two years is quite tough.

641
00:26:25,151 --> 00:26:26,486
I mean, before then...

642
00:26:30,123 --> 00:26:31,858
That was quite straightforward.

643
00:26:32,592 --> 00:26:34,060
- Is this it?
- This is the place.

644
00:26:34,060 --> 00:26:35,395
It must be inside.

645
00:26:35,395 --> 00:26:36,195
There it is.

646
00:26:36,195 --> 00:26:37,930
Where are you going? We aren't done.

647
00:26:38,564 --> 00:26:39,399
I have to go.

648
00:26:39,399 --> 00:26:41,267
Where are you going?

649
00:26:41,267 --> 00:26:42,835
To meet another man.

650
00:26:44,604 --> 00:26:46,039
Thanks for driving me.

651
00:26:46,539 --> 00:26:47,540
Have a good talk.

652
00:26:47,540 --> 00:26:48,941
I'll see you back at the lodging.

653
00:26:48,941 --> 00:26:50,309
Get there safely.

654
00:26:51,010 --> 00:26:52,045
This feels so strange.

655
00:26:52,045 --> 00:26:54,747
He's dropping her off for another date.

656
00:26:55,248 --> 00:26:56,416
(Jeong Yoon and Ye Chan's date)

657
00:26:56,416 --> 00:26:58,951
- The walking expert's pick.
- Okay.

658
00:27:02,055 --> 00:27:04,957
(Their date is at Andong Imcheonggak.)

659
00:27:04,957 --> 00:27:06,459
- Classic Andong.
- Andong.

660
00:27:06,459 --> 00:27:07,593
This place is nice too.

661
00:27:07,593 --> 00:27:09,595
Yes, I didn't know this was here.

662
00:27:11,698 --> 00:27:13,333
Should we sit there?

663
00:27:13,900 --> 00:27:16,669
It's Jeong Yoon and Ye Chan's
first one-on-one date.

664
00:27:16,669 --> 00:27:18,237
That took long enough.

665
00:27:19,272 --> 00:27:22,342
After our talk yesterday,

666
00:27:22,342 --> 00:27:24,510
did your feelings or thoughts change?

667
00:27:24,510 --> 00:27:25,978
Did you think it over today?

668
00:27:26,446 --> 00:27:28,648
While we talked yesterday,

669
00:27:28,648 --> 00:27:29,916
I realized I was right.

670
00:27:29,916 --> 00:27:33,586
I thought we'd really click
when I first saw you,

671
00:27:33,586 --> 00:27:35,054
and it turns out we do.

672
00:27:35,054 --> 00:27:37,156
Our banter works,

673
00:27:37,156 --> 00:27:38,124
and we have just the right...

674
00:27:38,124 --> 00:27:41,494
amount of playful cheekiness.

675
00:27:41,494 --> 00:27:43,396
That's a very polite way to put it.

676
00:27:43,396 --> 00:27:46,265
We have good chemistry.

677
00:27:46,265 --> 00:27:47,633
The truth is,

678
00:27:47,633 --> 00:27:49,268
your sense of humor...

679
00:27:49,268 --> 00:27:52,405
isn't something you change at our age.

680
00:27:52,405 --> 00:27:54,707
Either you click or you don't.

681
00:27:54,707 --> 00:27:56,109
And I think we click.

682
00:27:57,010 --> 00:27:59,545
We didn't talk for the first three days.

683
00:27:59,545 --> 00:28:00,279
Right.

684
00:28:00,279 --> 00:28:03,783
So I can only do what I can from here.

685
00:28:03,783 --> 00:28:07,553
I want to make more chances
for us to talk.

686
00:28:07,553 --> 00:28:09,789
Since we still have one day left.

687
00:28:09,789 --> 00:28:13,426
My answer is to give it my best.

688
00:28:14,727 --> 00:28:15,728
What do you think?

689
00:28:16,696 --> 00:28:20,133
Before we talked, I thought it was over.

690
00:28:20,133 --> 00:28:23,336
It felt like, "Well, goodbye."

691
00:28:23,336 --> 00:28:26,806
Now, I think there's more to consider.

692
00:28:26,806 --> 00:28:30,443
I want to see how well
we play off each other, as you said.

693
00:28:30,443 --> 00:28:33,579
I'm more comfortable now than yesterday,

694
00:28:33,579 --> 00:28:37,417
and even more than I was
at the café earlier.

695
00:28:37,417 --> 00:28:42,855
We're finally finding our rhythm.

696
00:28:42,855 --> 00:28:45,658
So I need time to sort out my thoughts.

697
00:28:45,658 --> 00:28:47,827
And I asked you everything I wanted to.

698
00:28:48,127 --> 00:28:49,929
Anyway, yesterday,

699
00:28:49,929 --> 00:28:52,932
I was so focused on you showing up
that I didn't get to tell you this.

700
00:28:52,932 --> 00:28:56,769
Your mother relayed it all very well,

701
00:28:57,370 --> 00:28:59,505
and I wanted to thank her for that too.

702
00:29:00,073 --> 00:29:01,741
That sounds like an acceptance speech.

703
00:29:01,741 --> 00:29:02,542
(Laughing)

704
00:29:02,542 --> 00:29:05,244
- I thought so too.
- I kept thinking that.

705
00:29:05,244 --> 00:29:08,081
And the long walk up isn't easy,

706
00:29:08,081 --> 00:29:09,082
as you know.

707
00:29:09,082 --> 00:29:10,049
It really is a long way.

708
00:29:10,049 --> 00:29:11,384
It is far.

709
00:29:11,384 --> 00:29:15,521
I bet so many women got out of breath...

710
00:29:15,521 --> 00:29:17,123
while climbing that hill.

711
00:29:17,890 --> 00:29:19,726
The doorstep is a little worn down.

712
00:29:20,293 --> 00:29:23,663
If my interest went up...

713
00:29:23,663 --> 00:29:25,198
twenty to 30 percent last night,

714
00:29:25,198 --> 00:29:26,966
it went up another 20 percent...

715
00:29:26,966 --> 00:29:29,335
during today's short date.

716
00:29:29,335 --> 00:29:32,005
That easy back-and-forth...

717
00:29:32,005 --> 00:29:33,506
was what I liked most.

718
00:29:33,506 --> 00:29:35,108
Twenty percent then and 20 percent now.

719
00:29:35,108 --> 00:29:37,176
Why bring up the worn doorstep...

720
00:29:37,176 --> 00:29:38,745
if you want to win Jeong Yoon over?

721
00:29:38,745 --> 00:29:41,881
Watch this show from the first episode.

722
00:29:41,881 --> 00:29:45,118
She was always his first choice.

723
00:29:45,118 --> 00:29:46,653
And it rose 20 percent yesterday?

724
00:29:46,653 --> 00:29:49,222
What was the original percentage, then?

725
00:29:49,222 --> 00:29:52,992
He's instinctively trying...

726
00:29:52,992 --> 00:29:54,293
to protect his pride.

727
00:29:54,761 --> 00:29:56,429
Let's choose a pasta to share.

728
00:29:56,429 --> 00:29:58,297
- Tomato.
- Tomato?

729
00:29:58,297 --> 00:30:01,601
At first, everyone told me...

730
00:30:01,601 --> 00:30:04,170
I was so kind and innocent.

731
00:30:04,170 --> 00:30:06,873
I didn't see myself that way,

732
00:30:06,873 --> 00:30:08,941
so I wondered what made them say it.

733
00:30:08,941 --> 00:30:11,044
Then my mind just ran with it.

734
00:30:11,044 --> 00:30:13,379
They're all at least six years older,
that's why.

735
00:30:13,379 --> 00:30:14,714
Is that so?

736
00:30:14,714 --> 00:30:16,582
You're eating with a man nine years older.

737
00:30:17,517 --> 00:30:19,118
How old is your department head?

738
00:30:19,552 --> 00:30:20,987
Can I be honest?

739
00:30:20,987 --> 00:30:22,989
The senior manager I find intimidating...

740
00:30:23,489 --> 00:30:25,391
- is the same age as you.
- I knew it.

741
00:30:25,391 --> 00:30:26,259
That's roughly the age difference.

742
00:30:26,259 --> 00:30:27,994
He sees her as a baby.

743
00:30:27,994 --> 00:30:30,630
I hadn't really felt the age gap before.

744
00:30:30,630 --> 00:30:32,565
Then I realized you were my manager's age.

745
00:30:32,565 --> 00:30:33,366
Exactly.

746
00:30:33,366 --> 00:30:34,434
And suddenly, it hit me.

747
00:30:34,434 --> 00:30:36,602
It is a pretty big gap.

748
00:30:36,602 --> 00:30:40,440
I've never eaten alone...

749
00:30:40,440 --> 00:30:43,543
with someone nine years younger.

750
00:30:45,712 --> 00:30:47,680
Even as you watch this,

751
00:30:47,680 --> 00:30:49,749
- you can see he's pushing her away.
- Right.

752
00:30:49,749 --> 00:30:51,884
If it were someone he truly loved,

753
00:30:51,884 --> 00:30:54,120
not a nine-year gap,
but even a 19-year gap...

754
00:30:54,120 --> 00:30:56,356
would make him find a way to bridge it.

755
00:30:56,356 --> 00:30:57,457
Right.

756
00:30:57,457 --> 00:30:59,492
But he's mentioning
the generation gap himself.

757
00:30:59,492 --> 00:31:01,661
I kept wondering...

758
00:31:02,729 --> 00:31:04,197
why you asked me to eat with you.

759
00:31:05,798 --> 00:31:09,435
I didn't choose you
for yesterday's date, right?

760
00:31:10,336 --> 00:31:12,405
I don't even know why,

761
00:31:12,405 --> 00:31:15,174
but it bothered me a little.

762
00:31:16,409 --> 00:31:17,577
That's why.

763
00:31:17,577 --> 00:31:20,013
I know the age gap matters.

764
00:31:20,947 --> 00:31:22,982
I understand all that,

765
00:31:24,083 --> 00:31:28,321
but you've been on my mind
from day one through day five.

766
00:31:29,088 --> 00:31:31,090
I think something is still there.

767
00:31:31,090 --> 00:31:32,725
I just wanted to...

768
00:31:32,725 --> 00:31:34,360
follow my heart.

769
00:31:34,360 --> 00:31:35,528
I can't quite explain it.

770
00:31:35,528 --> 00:31:37,430
I just followed what drew me in.

771
00:31:37,430 --> 00:31:39,132
I think that matters.

772
00:31:39,132 --> 00:31:40,700
So that's what I did.

773
00:31:42,702 --> 00:31:48,241
(In Kwon reflects on Do Yoon's feelings.)

774
00:31:49,909 --> 00:31:51,811
A nine-year gap.

775
00:31:54,013 --> 00:31:55,648
Nine years.

776
00:31:55,648 --> 00:31:56,949
She doesn't look pleased.

777
00:31:59,118 --> 00:32:00,920
The nine-year gap is hard for me,

778
00:32:02,622 --> 00:32:05,391
and I honestly can't get past it.

779
00:32:05,391 --> 00:32:06,225
Right.

780
00:32:07,360 --> 00:32:08,528
I understand.

781
00:32:09,095 --> 00:32:12,332
"Look at him obsessing over nine years."

782
00:32:12,332 --> 00:32:15,301
"Is that any way to treat
a younger woman?"

783
00:32:16,536 --> 00:32:17,904
This nine-year gap.

784
00:32:18,971 --> 00:32:19,972
Well,

785
00:32:20,506 --> 00:32:23,309
I think I need time to think.

786
00:32:24,377 --> 00:32:25,778
I'll think about it too.

787
00:32:26,813 --> 00:32:28,781
Excuse me,

788
00:32:28,781 --> 00:32:30,016
but anyone listening might think...

789
00:32:30,016 --> 00:32:31,985
Jeong Yoon and Do Yoon...

790
00:32:31,985 --> 00:32:33,519
were about ten years apart.

791
00:32:33,519 --> 00:32:36,589
- They're only three years apart.
- Three.

792
00:32:36,589 --> 00:32:38,024
He simply likes Jeong Yoon.

793
00:32:38,024 --> 00:32:39,726
Exactly.

794
00:32:39,726 --> 00:32:41,995
From Do Yoon's perspective,

795
00:32:41,995 --> 00:32:45,732
she asked him out first today
and told him she was interested.

796
00:32:45,732 --> 00:32:46,499
Right.

797
00:32:46,499 --> 00:32:48,568
But all she hears here is this.

798
00:32:48,568 --> 00:32:50,069
"A nine-year gap!"

799
00:32:50,069 --> 00:32:52,939
"I'm the same age as your manager!"

800
00:32:52,939 --> 00:32:56,776
I understand In Kwon's concerns.

801
00:32:56,776 --> 00:32:59,946
But if he keeps dwelling on their ages,

802
00:32:59,946 --> 00:33:02,749
from Do Yoon's perspective,

803
00:33:02,749 --> 00:33:04,150
- that has to hurt.
- Right.

804
00:33:05,785 --> 00:33:06,853
My...

805
00:33:10,023 --> 00:33:12,892
first choice is still Jeong Yoon.

806
00:33:15,828 --> 00:33:16,696
I see.

807
00:33:16,696 --> 00:33:20,933
So I really appreciated
that you asked me to eat with you.

808
00:33:23,036 --> 00:33:25,271
I'm glad I could be honest with you.

809
00:33:28,541 --> 00:33:30,443
She has nothing to say.

810
00:33:30,443 --> 00:33:34,247
I didn't want to lead her on.

811
00:33:34,247 --> 00:33:36,749
I still felt awful after saying it.

812
00:33:37,617 --> 00:33:39,419
He said Jeong Yoon was his first choice,

813
00:33:39,419 --> 00:33:43,289
and that our age gap worried him.

814
00:33:43,289 --> 00:33:45,358
I understood. I did,

815
00:33:46,359 --> 00:33:48,594
but it still hurt.

816
00:33:48,594 --> 00:33:49,562
Right.

817
00:33:50,163 --> 00:33:51,497
It hurt me too.

818
00:33:52,198 --> 00:33:53,232
Because I'm her age.

819
00:33:53,232 --> 00:33:56,869
I can't help wondering...

820
00:33:56,869 --> 00:33:58,571
if he could've phrased it differently.

821
00:33:58,571 --> 00:34:00,306
In a way, In Kwon...

822
00:34:00,306 --> 00:34:01,708
made his feelings very clear.

823
00:34:01,708 --> 00:34:03,476
Right. He was very clear.

824
00:34:04,210 --> 00:34:06,412
- Have you been waiting long?
- You look tired.

825
00:34:06,412 --> 00:34:07,146
A little.

826
00:34:07,146 --> 00:34:08,915
Thanks. Just a little.

827
00:34:08,915 --> 00:34:10,717
- Do you want something to drink?
- Yes.

828
00:34:11,017 --> 00:34:13,186
I really enjoyed the coffee this morning.

829
00:34:13,186 --> 00:34:14,520
- It was good, right?
- Yes.

830
00:34:14,520 --> 00:34:16,255
You really surprised me.

831
00:34:16,255 --> 00:34:17,757
Your mother seemed even more surprised.

832
00:34:17,757 --> 00:34:19,993
Now I understand what your note meant.

833
00:34:19,993 --> 00:34:22,328
"You'll be busy today."

834
00:34:22,328 --> 00:34:24,030
You saw the future.

835
00:34:24,030 --> 00:34:25,531
I didn't. I predicted it.

836
00:34:27,600 --> 00:34:30,503
It does feel like a lot of pressure.

837
00:34:30,503 --> 00:34:33,039
Until yesterday,

838
00:34:33,039 --> 00:34:35,708
I felt people showed interest quietly.

839
00:34:35,708 --> 00:34:38,644
Since this morning, all eyes are on me.

840
00:34:38,644 --> 00:34:40,380
"Whom will Jeong Yoon choose?"

841
00:34:40,380 --> 00:34:42,181
That's what it feels like.

842
00:34:42,181 --> 00:34:46,285
I didn't want to add to that pressure.

843
00:34:46,786 --> 00:34:48,454
Everyone else said the same thing.

844
00:34:48,454 --> 00:34:49,188
Really?

845
00:34:49,188 --> 00:34:50,823
I assumed those two...

846
00:34:50,823 --> 00:34:52,759
would've pushed forward like this.

847
00:34:52,759 --> 00:34:55,094
Everyone knows my personality now.

848
00:34:55,094 --> 00:34:57,830
They know I run when I feel pressured.

849
00:34:57,830 --> 00:34:59,932
Those two figured that out already?

850
00:35:01,467 --> 00:35:04,037
It took me three or four tries.

851
00:35:05,171 --> 00:35:06,673
They're quick to catch on.

852
00:35:09,042 --> 00:35:11,611
We've talked this much,

853
00:35:11,611 --> 00:35:14,280
so I think I've made...

854
00:35:14,280 --> 00:35:16,816
my thoughts and feelings...

855
00:35:16,816 --> 00:35:18,918
pretty clear to you.

856
00:35:18,918 --> 00:35:22,121
But the other two...

857
00:35:22,121 --> 00:35:24,357
are great guys, even from my perspective.

858
00:35:25,458 --> 00:35:29,095
You should talk to them too...

859
00:35:29,095 --> 00:35:30,363
before you make up your mind.

860
00:35:30,363 --> 00:35:34,000
If things do work out here,

861
00:35:34,000 --> 00:35:36,602
this goes beyond these five days.

862
00:35:36,602 --> 00:35:40,773
Take your time and decide for yourself.

863
00:35:41,974 --> 00:35:45,778
I felt In Kwon gave me room
to get to know the others...

864
00:35:45,778 --> 00:35:49,816
so I could choose with confidence.

865
00:35:49,816 --> 00:35:55,054
All three have very different styles,

866
00:35:55,054 --> 00:35:58,124
so I have more to consider now.

867
00:35:58,925 --> 00:36:03,629
After watching her talk with all three,

868
00:36:03,629 --> 00:36:06,099
I honestly don't know how she feels.

869
00:36:06,099 --> 00:36:07,533
My pick is Seong Mo.

870
00:36:08,167 --> 00:36:12,071
It felt most like a real date with him.

871
00:36:12,071 --> 00:36:13,206
The way they talked.

872
00:36:13,206 --> 00:36:13,973
They seemed comfortable.

873
00:36:13,973 --> 00:36:17,844
Still, In Kwon may have the advantage.

874
00:36:17,844 --> 00:36:19,946
Right, because they've talked the most.

875
00:36:19,946 --> 00:36:23,316
They've had the most time to grow close.

876
00:36:24,283 --> 00:36:25,218
(Meanwhile, sighs fill the house.)

877
00:36:25,218 --> 00:36:27,286
What are we supposed to do?

878
00:36:28,154 --> 00:36:32,191
Last night, she must've planned
to meet Shin Woo today.

879
00:36:32,792 --> 00:36:35,995
Da Hye brought up religion,
and he said he'll find faith.

880
00:36:35,995 --> 00:36:37,530
But that's because he's crazy about her.

881
00:36:37,530 --> 00:36:38,731
Of course.

882
00:36:39,232 --> 00:36:41,100
Kang Hyeon is over here.

883
00:36:41,100 --> 00:36:42,001
She's with the mothers.

884
00:36:42,001 --> 00:36:44,370
Has Kang Hyeon chosen
to be with the mothers now?

885
00:36:45,004 --> 00:36:46,939
But she isn't eating with her own mother.

886
00:36:46,939 --> 00:36:48,975
She's eating with the other mothers.

887
00:36:50,143 --> 00:36:51,811
Right, I've heard about that too.

888
00:36:51,811 --> 00:36:53,680
People promise they'll attend church,

889
00:36:53,680 --> 00:36:55,248
but almost no one follows through.

890
00:36:55,248 --> 00:36:57,116
- None.
- No one.

891
00:36:57,116 --> 00:36:59,419
If I were reborn and told to remarry,

892
00:36:59,419 --> 00:37:01,120
I wouldn't marry a nonbeliever.

893
00:37:01,120 --> 00:37:02,121
I'd rather not marry at all.

894
00:37:02,121 --> 00:37:04,190
- Goodness, that's firm.
- I mean it.

895
00:37:04,190 --> 00:37:07,093
That's why you want your daughter
to marry someone who shares her faith.

896
00:37:07,093 --> 00:37:08,461
Right. That's how I feel.

897
00:37:08,461 --> 00:37:10,330
- I understand you.
- Exactly.

898
00:37:10,330 --> 00:37:13,032
Faith matters so much when dating.

899
00:37:13,032 --> 00:37:15,501
For us, faith wasn't first priority.
It was priority zero.

900
00:37:15,501 --> 00:37:17,570
- You said that?
- Of course.

901
00:37:17,570 --> 00:37:18,671
We want a believer.

902
00:37:18,905 --> 00:37:22,375
Da Hye and Ye Chan's mom
really clicked yesterday.

903
00:37:22,375 --> 00:37:25,078
Da Hye even said, "Let's stay close."

904
00:37:25,078 --> 00:37:27,747
But Ye Chan's feelings are what matter.

905
00:37:27,747 --> 00:37:30,316
The moms are only third parties.

906
00:37:30,316 --> 00:37:31,384
Exactly.

907
00:37:31,918 --> 00:37:36,189
But Ye Chan's heart is with Jeong Yoon.

908
00:37:36,189 --> 00:37:37,290
She said...

909
00:37:37,290 --> 00:37:39,258
women like Jeong Yoon are his type.

910
00:37:39,258 --> 00:37:40,693
She's glamorous and pretty.

911
00:37:40,693 --> 00:37:42,662
But she doesn't share his faith.

912
00:37:42,662 --> 00:37:44,097
Ye Chan's mother and I...

913
00:37:44,097 --> 00:37:46,032
want to set our children up,

914
00:37:46,032 --> 00:37:47,800
but they don't feel the same way.

915
00:37:47,800 --> 00:37:48,801
You know?

916
00:37:48,801 --> 00:37:50,069
They keep missing each other.

917
00:37:50,403 --> 00:37:51,537
(Someone enters during their talk.)

918
00:37:51,537 --> 00:37:53,439
Welcome. Have you eaten?

919
00:37:54,165 --> 00:37:55,733
We only had cup noodles.

920
00:37:55,733 --> 00:37:56,768
(Jeong Yoon's mother appears.)

921
00:37:56,768 --> 00:37:58,369
Cup noodles. I'm already full.

922
00:37:59,571 --> 00:38:00,472
Is Jeong Yoon back?

923
00:38:00,472 --> 00:38:01,573
Not yet.

924
00:38:01,573 --> 00:38:03,741
Who did Jeong Yoon go out with today?

925
00:38:03,741 --> 00:38:05,543
Seong Mo, Ye Chan, and In Kwon.

926
00:38:05,543 --> 00:38:06,711
All three went out?

927
00:38:06,711 --> 00:38:08,780
No, not together. She's fully booked.

928
00:38:10,014 --> 00:38:10,982
"She's fully booked."

929
00:38:10,982 --> 00:38:12,817
Kang Hyeon is like...

930
00:38:12,817 --> 00:38:13,818
The one giving progress reports.

931
00:38:13,818 --> 00:38:17,388
She's like the mothers' little sister.

932
00:38:17,388 --> 00:38:22,060
You know, the one who explains it all?

933
00:38:22,060 --> 00:38:23,561
She relates to them so well.

934
00:38:23,561 --> 00:38:26,097
She's even speaking casually with them.

935
00:38:27,398 --> 00:38:29,901
What does Da Hye think of Ye Chan?

936
00:38:29,901 --> 00:38:31,603
Regardless of whether she likes him,

937
00:38:31,603 --> 00:38:33,738
they talked on the second or third day.

938
00:38:33,738 --> 00:38:35,440
- They talked?
- They did.

939
00:38:35,440 --> 00:38:38,877
But Ye Chan's mother and Da Hye clicked.

940
00:38:38,877 --> 00:38:41,913
Everything she said won Da Hye over.

941
00:38:41,913 --> 00:38:43,414
Completely.

942
00:38:43,414 --> 00:38:44,349
She was completely won over.

943
00:38:44,349 --> 00:38:46,351
Da Hye is exactly what she wants.

944
00:38:46,351 --> 00:38:47,619
She's her ideal daughter-in-law.

945
00:38:47,619 --> 00:38:49,487
She's exactly who his mother wants.

946
00:38:49,487 --> 00:38:51,156
The two get along perfectly.

947
00:38:51,156 --> 00:38:53,625
But the kids keep missing each other.

948
00:38:54,259 --> 00:38:55,527
They still haven't met.

949
00:38:55,527 --> 00:38:57,862
I told her to meet him today, but...

950
00:38:57,862 --> 00:38:59,898
- Shin Woo came first.
- He did again.

951
00:38:59,898 --> 00:39:02,100
Couldn't she bring him to church?

952
00:39:02,100 --> 00:39:02,967
Who?

953
00:39:03,334 --> 00:39:04,769
That won't be easy.

954
00:39:04,769 --> 00:39:08,206
Joining a religious family is harder.

955
00:39:08,206 --> 00:39:09,541
It's really difficult.

956
00:39:09,541 --> 00:39:12,210
Jeong Yoon asked about religion too.

957
00:39:12,210 --> 00:39:15,313
She said she asked Ye Chan about it.

958
00:39:15,313 --> 00:39:17,916
Ye Chan probably says it's fine for now.

959
00:39:17,916 --> 00:39:19,551
He says it's fine now.

960
00:39:19,551 --> 00:39:22,220
But it isn't that simple.

961
00:39:22,220 --> 00:39:23,288
Right.

962
00:39:23,288 --> 00:39:24,856
Nonbelievers wouldn't understand.

963
00:39:26,424 --> 00:39:29,227
- Thanks. See you later.
- See you.

964
00:39:29,227 --> 00:39:30,228
Da Hye is back.

965
00:39:30,728 --> 00:39:31,996
Hello, everyone.

966
00:39:31,996 --> 00:39:33,765
- Hello, ma'am.
- You did well today.

967
00:39:34,299 --> 00:39:35,133
See you later.

968
00:39:35,133 --> 00:39:36,501
Get home safely.

969
00:39:36,501 --> 00:39:37,702
Goodbye.

970
00:39:37,702 --> 00:39:39,971
Goodness, you must be exhausted.

971
00:39:39,971 --> 00:39:41,005
It must've been hard.

972
00:39:42,340 --> 00:39:43,308
You can turn off the light.

973
00:39:43,308 --> 00:39:45,009
Honestly,

974
00:39:45,009 --> 00:39:46,945
I just feel like...

975
00:39:47,312 --> 00:39:49,114
my romantic interest has faded a lot.

976
00:39:49,114 --> 00:39:50,682
It's not that I never felt anything.

977
00:39:50,682 --> 00:39:52,750
There were definitely moments I did.

978
00:39:52,750 --> 00:39:53,918
My goodness.

979
00:39:53,918 --> 00:39:56,020
But most of those feelings are gone now.

980
00:39:56,921 --> 00:40:00,558
Meet Ye Chan one last time.

981
00:40:00,558 --> 00:40:02,193
But there's no time left.

982
00:40:02,193 --> 00:40:03,495
Can't you meet today?

983
00:40:03,495 --> 00:40:05,830
Out of nowhere on the final day,

984
00:40:05,830 --> 00:40:07,198
you want me to approach Ye Chan now?

985
00:40:07,198 --> 00:40:08,500
But his mother came yesterday.

986
00:40:08,867 --> 00:40:12,570
And she picked you for the solo date.

987
00:40:12,570 --> 00:40:13,138
Well...

988
00:40:13,138 --> 00:40:15,340
From what I can tell, Da Hye's mother...

989
00:40:15,340 --> 00:40:18,910
really wants things to work with Ye Chan.

990
00:40:18,910 --> 00:40:22,347
She's making quite a case for him.

991
00:40:22,347 --> 00:40:25,383
But none of it really matters.

992
00:40:26,684 --> 00:40:28,453
Do Yoon, should we go outside and talk?

993
00:40:28,453 --> 00:40:30,822
- Yes.
- May I talk with Do Yoon?

994
00:40:31,322 --> 00:40:35,460
I narrowed my options down to In Kwon.

995
00:40:35,460 --> 00:40:36,795
It's In Kwon.

996
00:40:36,795 --> 00:40:39,831
We talked when we went out earlier.

997
00:40:39,831 --> 00:40:42,100
We're nine years apart, right?

998
00:40:42,100 --> 00:40:43,802
For that reason,

999
00:40:43,802 --> 00:40:45,837
I feel a lot of pressure,

1000
00:40:45,837 --> 00:40:48,173
and I thought he'd feel it too.

1001
00:40:48,173 --> 00:40:49,774
But that's only what you think.

1002
00:40:50,708 --> 00:40:53,545
I want you to focus on your own feelings.

1003
00:40:53,545 --> 00:40:55,013
What do you truly...

1004
00:40:55,013 --> 00:40:56,281
But...

1005
00:40:56,281 --> 00:40:58,216
I really did focus on my feelings.

1006
00:40:58,216 --> 00:40:59,117
You did?

1007
00:40:59,117 --> 00:41:02,821
I've followed only my heart so far.

1008
00:41:02,821 --> 00:41:04,656
I focused on what I felt.

1009
00:41:04,656 --> 00:41:06,724
That's how I made my choice.

1010
00:41:06,724 --> 00:41:08,460
I looked only at my own heart.

1011
00:41:08,460 --> 00:41:10,728
That's the absolute truth.

1012
00:41:10,728 --> 00:41:13,398
And after all that, you still had no one?

1013
00:41:13,398 --> 00:41:14,466
Right.

1014
00:41:15,033 --> 00:41:16,734
I wrote a lot on my own.

1015
00:41:16,734 --> 00:41:19,003
I kept asking myself how I really felt.

1016
00:41:19,003 --> 00:41:21,206
That's how I reached my conclusion.

1017
00:41:21,206 --> 00:41:22,774
Honestly, I was a little hurt.

1018
00:41:22,774 --> 00:41:24,742
- Why?
- I think I'll cry.

1019
00:41:24,742 --> 00:41:27,045
There's no tissue. Use your hand, like me.

1020
00:41:27,045 --> 00:41:33,718
(Do Yoon suddenly bursts into tears.)

1021
00:41:35,153 --> 00:41:36,154
Do you want to use this?

1022
00:41:37,622 --> 00:41:39,224
Use this. It's all right.

1023
00:41:40,158 --> 00:41:42,260
He put up such a wall.

1024
00:41:42,827 --> 00:41:44,195
I'm sad too.

1025
00:41:44,195 --> 00:41:46,731
It's all right. Go ahead and cry.

1026
00:41:46,731 --> 00:41:48,967
You must've been hurt. Let it out.

1027
00:41:53,671 --> 00:41:54,606
I'm sorry.

1028
00:41:54,606 --> 00:41:56,207
It's all right.

1029
00:41:57,342 --> 00:42:00,979
When everyone kept calling me cute...

1030
00:42:00,979 --> 00:42:02,080
I can see why you hated hearing it.

1031
00:42:02,080 --> 00:42:03,648
- It bothered me.
- I knew it.

1032
00:42:03,648 --> 00:42:06,017
- It seemed like they saw you as a baby.
- Right.

1033
00:42:06,017 --> 00:42:07,185
I can understand that.

1034
00:42:07,786 --> 00:42:09,320
It was really hard.

1035
00:42:09,320 --> 00:42:10,655
I see.

1036
00:42:12,257 --> 00:42:15,994
She was born in 1999,
and she's 28 this year.

1037
00:42:16,528 --> 00:42:18,129
No wonder she seemed like a baby.

1038
00:42:18,830 --> 00:42:20,832
In Kwon, she's far too young for you.

1039
00:42:21,332 --> 00:42:23,001
A nine-year gap.

1040
00:42:24,469 --> 00:42:25,904
Nine years.

1041
00:42:25,904 --> 00:42:28,039
What I heard most often here was...

1042
00:42:28,039 --> 00:42:29,908
that I seemed young, like a baby.

1043
00:42:29,908 --> 00:42:34,045
I never understood why.

1044
00:42:34,045 --> 00:42:37,015
I hated being called young,

1045
00:42:37,015 --> 00:42:39,584
and couldn't see why I heard it so often.

1046
00:42:39,584 --> 00:42:43,087
It all became too much emotionally.

1047
00:42:43,888 --> 00:42:45,023
(Her peer feels upset too.)

1048
00:42:45,023 --> 00:42:47,659
She's 28 years old.

1049
00:42:47,659 --> 00:42:48,927
She's almost 30.

1050
00:42:48,927 --> 00:42:51,095
Right. My mom had me at 25.

1051
00:42:51,095 --> 00:42:53,565
She's been working for years too.

1052
00:42:53,565 --> 00:42:57,268
Why should she come here
and be judged so harshly for her age?

1053
00:42:57,268 --> 00:42:59,704
I don't understand it.

1054
00:42:59,704 --> 00:43:01,172
She's been an adult for nine years.

1055
00:43:01,172 --> 00:43:02,140
Here's the problem.

1056
00:43:02,140 --> 00:43:05,677
Lee In Kwon made the age gap weird.
That's what happened.

1057
00:43:06,311 --> 00:43:08,880
(The final dinner arrives.)

1058
00:43:08,880 --> 00:43:10,248
That looks delicious.

1059
00:43:10,248 --> 00:43:11,549
Steamed crab? No.

1060
00:43:11,549 --> 00:43:14,352
It's their last dinner.

1061
00:43:14,886 --> 00:43:15,954
Braised monkfish.

1062
00:43:15,954 --> 00:43:16,921
That looks good.

1063
00:43:17,122 --> 00:43:19,491
The mothers are sitting separately.

1064
00:43:19,491 --> 00:43:21,159
Why is everyone sitting apart?

1065
00:43:21,159 --> 00:43:22,760
Are we sitting separately from the moms?

1066
00:43:24,362 --> 00:43:26,498
(Hesitates)

1067
00:43:26,865 --> 00:43:28,433
Thanks for the food.

1068
00:43:28,433 --> 00:43:29,501
Everyone, take some rice first.

1069
00:43:29,501 --> 00:43:31,069
(The men hesitate to sit down.)

1070
00:43:31,069 --> 00:43:32,103
No.

1071
00:43:32,103 --> 00:43:36,207
(In Kwon naturally sits
across from Jeong Yoon.)

1072
00:43:36,908 --> 00:43:39,477
(Looks around)

1073
00:43:41,212 --> 00:43:42,781
Ye Chan, come sit here and talk.

1074
00:43:42,781 --> 00:43:43,815
Should I?

1075
00:43:45,350 --> 00:43:46,217
What?

1076
00:43:47,886 --> 00:43:50,989
(Her mother watches Ye Chan and Da Hye.)

1077
00:43:50,989 --> 00:43:53,525
I kept a close eye on Ye Chan.

1078
00:43:53,525 --> 00:43:55,326
I watched to see if he'd sit with Da Hye.

1079
00:43:55,326 --> 00:43:59,297
I glanced back several times to check.

1080
00:44:00,165 --> 00:44:04,068
(She loves his choice of seat.)

1081
00:44:04,702 --> 00:44:07,071
(Shin Woo returns after stepping away.)

1082
00:44:07,071 --> 00:44:09,107
This had fallen.

1083
00:44:09,107 --> 00:44:10,542
I noticed it was missing.

1084
00:44:15,013 --> 00:44:18,183
(He walks past Da Hye...)

1085
00:44:18,183 --> 00:44:20,552
(and sits beside Do Yoon.)

1086
00:44:20,552 --> 00:44:22,053
Look at him.

1087
00:44:22,053 --> 00:44:23,621
I was like, "I can't."

1088
00:44:25,423 --> 00:44:27,525
- No.
- Do you want to share?

1089
00:44:27,525 --> 00:44:28,726
To avoid making Da Hye...

1090
00:44:30,261 --> 00:44:32,130
feel any pressure,

1091
00:44:32,130 --> 00:44:34,299
I sat down beside Do Yoon.

1092
00:44:35,066 --> 00:44:36,801
Could he and Do Yoon somehow...

1093
00:44:36,801 --> 00:44:38,503
start something new?

1094
00:44:38,503 --> 00:44:39,971
Let me see.

1095
00:44:39,971 --> 00:44:43,174
They're only seven years apart.

1096
00:44:43,174 --> 00:44:46,177
They may as well start something new.

1097
00:44:46,177 --> 00:44:49,247
I'd like that. I'm done with this mess.

1098
00:44:49,247 --> 00:44:50,648
(He sympathizes with Shin Woo.)

1099
00:44:52,984 --> 00:44:53,985
How was your date?

1100
00:44:53,985 --> 00:44:56,121
I talked to you the least.

1101
00:44:56,121 --> 00:44:57,522
Right. We barely talked.

1102
00:44:57,522 --> 00:44:59,290
With the others...

1103
00:44:59,290 --> 00:45:01,559
- Sorry, I have food in my mouth.
- Take your time.

1104
00:45:01,559 --> 00:45:04,863
We exercised and had coffee upstairs.

1105
00:45:04,863 --> 00:45:06,431
At the café upstairs?

1106
00:45:06,431 --> 00:45:07,866
We were allowed to go to that café?

1107
00:45:07,866 --> 00:45:09,701
It opens at 8 a.m. after our workout.

1108
00:45:11,002 --> 00:45:12,904
I was still fast asleep then.

1109
00:45:14,038 --> 00:45:15,340
I usually woke up around 9 a.m.

1110
00:45:15,340 --> 00:45:18,543
No wonder. It's so busy up there.

1111
00:45:18,543 --> 00:45:20,979
Let's talk, then. I regret that we didn't.

1112
00:45:20,979 --> 00:45:24,449
You may be the person
I talked to the least.

1113
00:45:24,449 --> 00:45:25,950
Really?

1114
00:45:25,950 --> 00:45:27,485
Honestly, I felt a little jealous.

1115
00:45:27,485 --> 00:45:28,686
Really?

1116
00:45:28,686 --> 00:45:31,856
Da Hye kept talking with Ye Chan,

1117
00:45:32,791 --> 00:45:35,326
and it kept bothering me.

1118
00:45:35,326 --> 00:45:36,895
My mind was a complete mess.

1119
00:45:45,069 --> 00:45:45,937
My goodness.

1120
00:45:45,937 --> 00:45:47,238
I doubt he even knows what he's eating.

1121
00:45:47,238 --> 00:45:50,708
This is painful to watch.

1122
00:45:51,442 --> 00:45:55,547
(The confusing final dinner ends.)

1123
00:45:55,747 --> 00:45:57,348
She had a misunderstanding, Mom.

1124
00:45:57,348 --> 00:45:58,082
About what?

1125
00:45:58,082 --> 00:45:58,983
Your tears.

1126
00:45:58,983 --> 00:46:00,385
Da Hye did?

1127
00:46:00,385 --> 00:46:01,486
I said I cried because I was happy.

1128
00:46:01,486 --> 00:46:02,987
Exactly. But she thought...

1129
00:46:03,288 --> 00:46:06,891
your tears meant something else.

1130
00:46:06,891 --> 00:46:08,893
I thought you'd end up sitting alone.

1131
00:46:08,893 --> 00:46:10,495
That's what I told her too.

1132
00:46:10,495 --> 00:46:14,799
She thought my parents disliked her.

1133
00:46:14,799 --> 00:46:16,835
She said that was weighing on her.

1134
00:46:17,735 --> 00:46:18,970
That's what she said.

1135
00:46:19,537 --> 00:46:22,974
Not at all. Mine were tears of joy.

1136
00:46:22,974 --> 00:46:24,909
She totally misunderstood you.

1137
00:46:24,909 --> 00:46:27,912
I thought I'd eased her worries
about religion...

1138
00:46:27,912 --> 00:46:30,849
because I explained it well.

1139
00:46:30,849 --> 00:46:32,784
I thought I'd put that to rest.

1140
00:46:32,784 --> 00:46:36,187
But now she fears
you and Father may dislike her.

1141
00:46:36,187 --> 00:46:40,225
But we had such a great talk yesterday.

1142
00:46:41,526 --> 00:46:43,428
But right now, I just...

1143
00:46:43,428 --> 00:46:46,965
We aren't that kind of family at all.

1144
00:46:46,965 --> 00:46:49,334
You said you told her that too.

1145
00:46:49,334 --> 00:46:50,568
I told her yesterday.

1146
00:46:50,568 --> 00:46:52,170
You did, but she still misunderstood.

1147
00:46:52,170 --> 00:46:55,773
I told Da Hye's mother
that I cried, and that she should cry too.

1148
00:46:55,773 --> 00:46:58,343
But I can see why she felt that way.

1149
00:46:58,343 --> 00:47:01,946
Her mother chose me,

1150
00:47:01,946 --> 00:47:04,983
while you told me to meet others.

1151
00:47:04,983 --> 00:47:07,852
But she went to someone else too
for the first-impression date.

1152
00:47:07,852 --> 00:47:09,487
- She didn't choose my son.
- Only at first.

1153
00:47:09,487 --> 00:47:12,991
I was in the same boat either way.

1154
00:47:12,991 --> 00:47:13,792
Right.

1155
00:47:13,792 --> 00:47:15,326
That isn't the problem right now.

1156
00:47:15,326 --> 00:47:17,195
She went somewhere else too.

1157
00:47:17,762 --> 00:47:20,298
Shin Woo seems...

1158
00:47:20,298 --> 00:47:23,768
a little inexperienced...

1159
00:47:23,768 --> 00:47:25,503
at reading a woman's feelings.

1160
00:47:25,503 --> 00:47:27,739
He does, because...

1161
00:47:27,739 --> 00:47:31,843
her words, face, and eyes...

1162
00:47:31,843 --> 00:47:36,614
should've told him she wasn't interested.

1163
00:47:36,614 --> 00:47:39,317
But from what he's saying to his mom,

1164
00:47:39,317 --> 00:47:43,488
he still thinks it's religion...

1165
00:47:43,488 --> 00:47:47,492
or something his mom said earlier.

1166
00:47:47,492 --> 00:47:48,593
It's sad to watch.

1167
00:47:50,028 --> 00:47:51,729
I really didn't mean to do that.

1168
00:47:51,729 --> 00:47:53,364
Mom, didn't you know this was happening?

1169
00:47:53,364 --> 00:47:54,599
- I didn't.
- That it was headed here?

1170
00:47:54,599 --> 00:47:57,368
- Think about it.
- Nobody ever told me.

1171
00:47:57,368 --> 00:47:59,838
You never picked her even once.

1172
00:47:59,838 --> 00:48:03,308
She and her mom picked me in the end.

1173
00:48:04,309 --> 00:48:06,144
I picked her every single time.

1174
00:48:06,144 --> 00:48:07,745
But you never picked her once.

1175
00:48:08,313 --> 00:48:10,148
Is he blaming his mother now?

1176
00:48:10,715 --> 00:48:13,084
Why did you suddenly change your mind?

1177
00:48:13,084 --> 00:48:15,320
Why did you switch to Choi Jeong Yoon?

1178
00:48:15,320 --> 00:48:16,187
When did I ever switch?

1179
00:48:16,187 --> 00:48:18,289
- Why switch to Choi Jeong Yoon?
- When did I?

1180
00:48:18,289 --> 00:48:19,757
Your choice two days ago.

1181
00:48:19,757 --> 00:48:22,460
(His mother's choice two days ago)

1182
00:48:22,827 --> 00:48:24,562
It was nothing serious.

1183
00:48:24,562 --> 00:48:26,231
- I switched to Choi Jeong Yoon?
- You did.

1184
00:48:26,231 --> 00:48:28,032
- What's wrong with him?
- Why switch?

1185
00:48:28,032 --> 00:48:30,068
What is wrong with him?

1186
00:48:30,068 --> 00:48:32,670
Why is he cornering his innocent mother...

1187
00:48:32,904 --> 00:48:34,572
and blaming her like this?

1188
00:48:34,572 --> 00:48:36,708
She's so confused. "I did that?"

1189
00:48:36,708 --> 00:48:38,143
It was nothing serious.

1190
00:48:38,143 --> 00:48:40,545
- I switched to Choi Jeong Yoon?
- You did.

1191
00:48:40,545 --> 00:48:41,513
Why did you switch to her?

1192
00:48:41,513 --> 00:48:42,914
I said afterward that it wasn't true.

1193
00:48:42,914 --> 00:48:45,350
But the misunderstanding has snowballed.

1194
00:48:45,350 --> 00:48:46,518
Then talk to her and clear it up.

1195
00:48:46,518 --> 00:48:47,852
I said I leaned that way until day two.

1196
00:48:47,852 --> 00:48:48,920
But the misunderstanding keeps growing.

1197
00:48:48,920 --> 00:48:51,890
I said yesterday I changed by day two.

1198
00:48:51,890 --> 00:48:55,026
Then explain it properly and clear it up.

1199
00:48:55,360 --> 00:48:58,229
All the mothers say it,
including Jeong Yoon's mother.

1200
00:48:58,229 --> 00:49:00,131
They call you the guy who goes all in.

1201
00:49:00,131 --> 00:49:03,568
Letting that sway you would be wrong.

1202
00:49:03,568 --> 00:49:04,702
I mean, to me...

1203
00:49:04,702 --> 00:49:06,538
What about that? I said I'd handle it.

1204
00:49:06,538 --> 00:49:09,140
- What?
- I said I'd handle it.

1205
00:49:09,140 --> 00:49:10,909
If I said I'll handle it,
why care what others call me?

1206
00:49:10,909 --> 00:49:12,577
He's completely lost his composure.

1207
00:49:14,078 --> 00:49:15,980
Did I ever say I cared?

1208
00:49:15,980 --> 00:49:18,650
I only said I just found out.

1209
00:49:18,650 --> 00:49:19,818
Get a grip.

1210
00:49:19,818 --> 00:49:21,786
Do you think I'm not flustered right now?

1211
00:49:25,924 --> 00:49:28,560
Fine. I won't say anything else.

1212
00:49:33,698 --> 00:49:35,967
Shin Woo has lost his composure.

1213
00:49:35,967 --> 00:49:37,068
Completely.

1214
00:49:37,068 --> 00:49:38,670
He's grasping for excuses now.

1215
00:49:38,670 --> 00:49:41,840
Things aren't going the way he wanted,

1216
00:49:41,840 --> 00:49:43,241
so he's lost his composure.

1217
00:49:43,241 --> 00:49:45,710
He's even saying...

1218
00:49:45,710 --> 00:49:47,145
all kinds of things to his mother.

1219
00:49:47,145 --> 00:49:48,913
Isn't he usually a devoted son?

1220
00:49:48,913 --> 00:49:50,615
- He is.
- But suddenly...

1221
00:49:50,615 --> 00:49:52,817
He's using his mother as an excuse.

1222
00:49:52,817 --> 00:49:54,052
Why is he treating her that way?

1223
00:49:54,052 --> 00:49:55,954
This isn't his mother's fault.

1224
00:49:55,954 --> 00:50:01,092
Da Hye simply isn't
that romantically attracted...

1225
00:50:01,092 --> 00:50:03,328
to Shin Woo.

1226
00:50:03,328 --> 00:50:04,996
There's no other reason.

1227
00:50:06,297 --> 00:50:09,267
(An alert sounds in the house.)

1228
00:50:09,734 --> 00:50:12,504
Tomorrow is the final choice.

1229
00:50:13,037 --> 00:50:16,908
We have an important announcement
before the final choice.

1230
00:50:17,509 --> 00:50:20,979
The children will choose first.

1231
00:50:20,979 --> 00:50:24,115
Both mothers must approve
of their children's choices...

1232
00:50:24,115 --> 00:50:26,151
for them to become a final couple.

1233
00:50:27,385 --> 00:50:29,053
On Match to Marry: With Parents 2,

1234
00:50:29,053 --> 00:50:31,122
even if the children choose each other,

1235
00:50:31,122 --> 00:50:34,459
both mothers must also approve...

1236
00:50:34,459 --> 00:50:36,661
for them to become a final couple.

1237
00:50:36,661 --> 00:50:38,530
If even one mother objects,

1238
00:50:38,530 --> 00:50:41,266
they cannot become a final couple.

1239
00:50:42,600 --> 00:50:44,402
My goodness.

1240
00:50:45,870 --> 00:50:47,672
This is intense.

1241
00:50:48,740 --> 00:50:51,276
(Sighs)

1242
00:50:51,276 --> 00:50:54,846
We will now begin the final interviews.

1243
00:50:56,014 --> 00:50:56,815
The final interviews?

1244
00:50:56,815 --> 00:50:59,918
The mothers must choose someone...

1245
00:50:59,918 --> 00:51:02,120
other than their own child.

1246
00:51:02,120 --> 00:51:04,422
Choose the one person...

1247
00:51:04,422 --> 00:51:06,391
you want to speak with one last time.

1248
00:51:07,158 --> 00:51:10,161
Dong Young kept wanting to talk to you.

1249
00:51:11,162 --> 00:51:13,164
There's no one I want to talk to.

1250
00:51:13,998 --> 00:51:15,300
I won't do it.

1251
00:51:15,767 --> 00:51:17,202
She's made up her mind.

1252
00:51:17,202 --> 00:51:20,104
What don't you like about
a pharmaceutical sales representative?

1253
00:51:20,104 --> 00:51:21,372
You said you dislike his job.

1254
00:51:22,707 --> 00:51:24,142
I just don't like it.

1255
00:51:25,343 --> 00:51:26,678
How can you say that?

1256
00:51:28,313 --> 00:51:30,115
She's very firm.

1257
00:51:30,882 --> 00:51:31,716
Goodness.

1258
00:51:31,716 --> 00:51:33,685
- At least talk to him.
- Ma'am.

1259
00:51:33,685 --> 00:51:36,154
It seems Ha Yoon's mother...

1260
00:51:36,154 --> 00:51:38,256
isn't only worried about the distance.

1261
00:51:38,256 --> 00:51:41,326
It seems she dislikes
Dong Young's job too.

1262
00:51:42,360 --> 00:51:45,196
In her generation,

1263
00:51:45,196 --> 00:51:49,734
there may still be some bias...

1264
00:51:49,734 --> 00:51:52,003
against sales jobs.

1265
00:51:52,003 --> 00:51:53,138
I just don't like it.

1266
00:51:54,405 --> 00:51:55,607
How can you say that?

1267
00:51:57,208 --> 00:51:59,744
(At the same time,
Dong Young's mother is deep in thought.)

1268
00:51:59,744 --> 00:52:02,213
Talk to whoever you want, Mom.

1269
00:52:02,914 --> 00:52:04,048
This is the last chance.

1270
00:52:05,316 --> 00:52:07,685
It doesn't have to be one of the guys.

1271
00:52:07,685 --> 00:52:09,454
You could talk to one of their mothers.

1272
00:52:09,454 --> 00:52:11,589
You've already talked with two men.

1273
00:52:11,589 --> 00:52:14,926
You could choose someone you haven't met.

1274
00:52:15,426 --> 00:52:18,229
You met In Kwon and Ye Chan
but not Seong Mo.

1275
00:52:18,229 --> 00:52:19,364
I don't really feel like it.

1276
00:52:20,265 --> 00:52:21,199
You don't?

1277
00:52:22,033 --> 00:52:24,502
Should I meet Da Hye or her mother?

1278
00:52:24,502 --> 00:52:25,703
Of course, meeting Da Hye is better.

1279
00:52:25,703 --> 00:52:27,071
It's better to talk with her directly.

1280
00:52:27,071 --> 00:52:29,340
I need to tell her I'm not opposed.

1281
00:52:29,340 --> 00:52:31,142
(His mother hopes to clear things up.)

1282
00:52:31,142 --> 00:52:32,310
This is heartbreaking.

1283
00:52:32,610 --> 00:52:35,246
She likes chocolate,
so take some or something like that.

1284
00:52:35,246 --> 00:52:36,548
Don't.

1285
00:52:37,048 --> 00:52:38,716
(Springs up)

1286
00:52:39,951 --> 00:52:41,986
(Shin Woo packs something else.)

1287
00:52:41,986 --> 00:52:45,156
I hope I get a chance to win Da Hye over.

1288
00:52:45,156 --> 00:52:48,460
I gathered everything I'd brought,

1289
00:52:48,460 --> 00:52:51,095
like pain relief patches for my knees,

1290
00:52:51,095 --> 00:52:54,265
herbal tonics, and antacids.

1291
00:52:55,133 --> 00:52:57,769
I packed it all up...

1292
00:52:57,769 --> 00:53:01,439
since I couldn't go out to buy a gift.

1293
00:53:01,439 --> 00:53:03,107
I did whatever I could...

1294
00:53:03,107 --> 00:53:05,310
to show her how I felt.

1295
00:53:06,311 --> 00:53:07,745
(His mother takes gifts to meet Da Hye.)

1296
00:53:07,745 --> 00:53:09,714
She's carrying quite a load.

1297
00:53:10,882 --> 00:53:13,885
No.

1298
00:53:14,686 --> 00:53:16,087
Actually, that's fair.

1299
00:53:16,087 --> 00:53:20,225
Shin Woo can only do his very best now.

1300
00:53:20,225 --> 00:53:22,060
But what makes me angry is,

1301
00:53:22,060 --> 00:53:23,228
why does his mother have to do it?

1302
00:53:23,228 --> 00:53:24,429
Right. He can't go through his mother.

1303
00:53:24,429 --> 00:53:25,997
Why is he taking it out on her?

1304
00:53:25,997 --> 00:53:28,967
If his mother meets Da Hye...

1305
00:53:28,967 --> 00:53:30,668
and starts doing all that,

1306
00:53:30,668 --> 00:53:34,139
she'll probably be even more horrified.

1307
00:53:35,607 --> 00:53:40,512
(The mothers hold final interviews
in the final evening.)

1308
00:53:41,446 --> 00:53:44,482
They must have so much on their minds.

1309
00:53:44,482 --> 00:53:45,917
It's their last chance to talk.

1310
00:53:48,419 --> 00:53:50,922
(Shin Woo's mother asks to meet first.)

1311
00:53:50,922 --> 00:53:52,590
- How have you been?
- You're tired, right?

1312
00:53:52,590 --> 00:53:55,260
Everyone seems tired...

1313
00:53:55,260 --> 00:53:57,195
after five days.

1314
00:53:57,195 --> 00:53:59,330
- You looked unwell earlier.
- Me?

1315
00:54:00,478 --> 00:54:02,814
She got dragged out again.

1316
00:54:03,615 --> 00:54:04,649
How is your neck?

1317
00:54:04,649 --> 00:54:05,683
It's fine.

1318
00:54:05,683 --> 00:54:07,352
Can you lift your neck like this?

1319
00:54:07,352 --> 00:54:09,053
Yes, it can.

1320
00:54:09,053 --> 00:54:10,321
Thankfully,

1321
00:54:10,321 --> 00:54:12,223
I got so much help from Shin Woo...

1322
00:54:12,223 --> 00:54:14,759
and from Ha Yoon too.

1323
00:54:14,759 --> 00:54:17,095
My knees bothered me before I came here.

1324
00:54:17,095 --> 00:54:18,630
I see.

1325
00:54:18,630 --> 00:54:19,864
I have some pain relief gel.

1326
00:54:19,864 --> 00:54:22,700
I wanted to give it to you.

1327
00:54:22,700 --> 00:54:24,335
I used it once.
Can I still give it to you?

1328
00:54:24,335 --> 00:54:25,603
No, I'm fine. Really.

1329
00:54:25,603 --> 00:54:26,871
I brought it.

1330
00:54:26,871 --> 00:54:28,840
- I see.
- I brought it here.

1331
00:54:28,840 --> 00:54:30,408
Ma'am, if you give it to me...

1332
00:54:30,408 --> 00:54:31,509
This is...

1333
00:54:32,744 --> 00:54:34,779
About this bag...

1334
00:54:34,779 --> 00:54:36,781
It may not look like much.

1335
00:54:36,781 --> 00:54:37,815
No, it seems very special.

1336
00:54:37,815 --> 00:54:39,250
It may not look like much, but no.

1337
00:54:39,250 --> 00:54:41,486
Shin Woo's father's best friend...

1338
00:54:41,486 --> 00:54:46,457
immigrated to the United States,

1339
00:54:46,457 --> 00:54:48,827
and his wife...

1340
00:54:48,827 --> 00:54:51,496
waited in line to buy this.

1341
00:54:51,496 --> 00:54:53,064
All that effort for this bag.

1342
00:54:53,064 --> 00:54:54,532
I brought this bag for you.

1343
00:54:54,532 --> 00:54:56,167
This isn't much,

1344
00:54:56,167 --> 00:54:58,069
but here's the gel too. Look.

1345
00:54:59,504 --> 00:55:01,940
Apply this if it hurts.

1346
00:55:01,940 --> 00:55:04,709
I'd really love to take it,

1347
00:55:04,709 --> 00:55:06,578
but your knees haven't fully healed yet.

1348
00:55:06,578 --> 00:55:08,479
It's fine. My knees are much better.

1349
00:55:08,479 --> 00:55:10,248
And we're going home tomorrow anyway.

1350
00:55:10,248 --> 00:55:11,216
I have plenty at home.

1351
00:55:11,216 --> 00:55:14,352
I can turn my neck all the way around,
a full 360 degrees.

1352
00:55:14,352 --> 00:55:16,654
Her neck turns just fine.

1353
00:55:16,921 --> 00:55:20,291
This is an herbal tonic.

1354
00:55:20,291 --> 00:55:22,494
- Share it with your mother.
- Please, ma'am.

1355
00:55:22,494 --> 00:55:26,397
That'll only make her feel more pressured.

1356
00:55:27,065 --> 00:55:29,200
I heard you liked chocolate.

1357
00:55:29,200 --> 00:55:31,169
Shin Woo's dad bought it last night.

1358
00:55:31,169 --> 00:55:32,537
Ma'am.

1359
00:55:32,537 --> 00:55:33,938
This is herbal digestive aid.

1360
00:55:33,938 --> 00:55:35,073
Ma'am.

1361
00:55:35,073 --> 00:55:36,374
Please take this.

1362
00:55:36,374 --> 00:55:37,876
What do we do?

1363
00:55:37,876 --> 00:55:40,178
She's trying so hard.

1364
00:55:40,178 --> 00:55:43,515
After her son made a scene
at the very end...

1365
00:55:43,515 --> 00:55:45,450
She got caught in the fallout.

1366
00:55:45,450 --> 00:55:49,254
She wasn't like this before.

1367
00:55:49,254 --> 00:55:52,557
Now she's unpacking everything...

1368
00:55:52,557 --> 00:55:54,526
and explaining each item.

1369
00:55:54,526 --> 00:55:56,728
- It's so sad.
- It's heartbreaking.

1370
00:55:57,428 --> 00:55:58,963
Da Hye.

1371
00:55:58,963 --> 00:56:00,632
Please take these with a smile, okay?

1372
00:56:01,666 --> 00:56:04,035
That's why I packed them.

1373
00:56:04,035 --> 00:56:07,539
This time, our roles are reversed.

1374
00:56:09,240 --> 00:56:11,643
The situation has changed.

1375
00:56:12,010 --> 00:56:13,178
Why are you crying?

1376
00:56:13,178 --> 00:56:15,513
You hugged me yesterday, remember?

1377
00:56:15,513 --> 00:56:16,781
I'll hug you today.

1378
00:56:16,781 --> 00:56:19,250
Let me hug you.

1379
00:56:19,250 --> 00:56:20,285
Thank you.

1380
00:56:20,285 --> 00:56:21,686
Goodness.

1381
00:56:23,721 --> 00:56:24,656
I'm sorry.

1382
00:56:24,656 --> 00:56:25,723
Why are you sorry?

1383
00:56:25,723 --> 00:56:28,326
I was the one crying like that yesterday.

1384
00:56:28,827 --> 00:56:30,361
They are tears of joy, right?

1385
00:56:31,429 --> 00:56:32,397
No.

1386
00:56:33,832 --> 00:56:35,466
Honestly,

1387
00:56:36,167 --> 00:56:39,003
I never cared about religion.

1388
00:56:39,304 --> 00:56:40,605
Here's how I see it.

1389
00:56:40,605 --> 00:56:45,844
What matters is how two people feel.

1390
00:56:46,177 --> 00:56:49,981
Shin Woo could go to church with you.

1391
00:56:51,115 --> 00:56:53,484
Why not? What's stopping...

1392
00:56:53,484 --> 00:56:58,122
Is there some reason he can't?

1393
00:56:58,122 --> 00:56:59,424
There isn't.

1394
00:56:59,424 --> 00:57:03,361
If you two connect, you can go together.

1395
00:57:04,529 --> 00:57:06,998
Shin Woo said he wouldn't mind.

1396
00:57:07,866 --> 00:57:09,934
Goodness, this is...

1397
00:57:10,702 --> 00:57:13,771
Watching this is heartbreaking.

1398
00:57:13,771 --> 00:57:16,908
If we aren't honest from the start,

1399
00:57:16,908 --> 00:57:18,810
this is what happens at the end.

1400
00:57:18,810 --> 00:57:20,011
People end up hurting in the end.

1401
00:57:20,011 --> 00:57:23,248
- It only gets harder.
- Right.

1402
00:57:24,082 --> 00:57:25,717
You two can work at it together.

1403
00:57:26,885 --> 00:57:33,157
Since coming here, I've realized...

1404
00:57:34,492 --> 00:57:36,528
my judgment can still be...

1405
00:57:38,163 --> 00:57:40,698
immature at times.

1406
00:57:40,698 --> 00:57:45,003
I may sound disrespectful,
so let me apologize first.

1407
00:57:45,003 --> 00:57:46,471
I'm sorry.

1408
00:57:53,811 --> 00:57:57,515
It's not because Shin Woo lacks anything.

1409
00:57:57,749 --> 00:58:00,084
I've really searched my heart...

1410
00:58:00,084 --> 00:58:03,821
to see whether it was ready
to keep this going outside.

1411
00:58:03,821 --> 00:58:07,091
I spent a lot of time thinking about it.

1412
00:58:07,091 --> 00:58:09,494
If I wasn't certain,

1413
00:58:09,494 --> 00:58:12,463
but chose him in the end anyway,

1414
00:58:12,730 --> 00:58:15,066
we could hurt each other even more.

1415
00:58:15,066 --> 00:58:18,903
It might also give him false hope.

1416
00:58:18,903 --> 00:58:23,341
His father happened to mention that
in our conversation yesterday.

1417
00:58:23,341 --> 00:58:25,610
If a relationship doesn't seem right,

1418
00:58:25,610 --> 00:58:29,047
he believes it's best to end it quickly.

1419
00:58:29,047 --> 00:58:31,249
To be honest,

1420
00:58:31,249 --> 00:58:33,852
after our date today,

1421
00:58:33,852 --> 00:58:36,955
I had mostly made up my mind.

1422
00:58:36,955 --> 00:58:37,922
I see.

1423
00:58:37,922 --> 00:58:38,923
So...

1424
00:58:38,923 --> 00:58:42,126
But you were trying
to help things work out.

1425
00:58:42,126 --> 00:58:45,797
Right. You're my first choice, Da Hye.

1426
00:58:45,797 --> 00:58:47,799
And Shin Woo told me...

1427
00:58:47,799 --> 00:58:51,703
he only talks about me in interviews.

1428
00:58:52,370 --> 00:58:55,507
He came on too strong and pressured you.

1429
00:58:56,140 --> 00:58:57,108
Isn't that right?

1430
00:58:59,043 --> 00:59:00,545
So...

1431
00:59:00,545 --> 00:59:02,380
though I'm truly grateful,

1432
00:59:02,981 --> 00:59:07,819
I'm sorry to tell you this.

1433
00:59:07,819 --> 00:59:10,121
I'm so sorry to say it on the last day.

1434
00:59:17,662 --> 00:59:20,131
If I say any more,

1435
00:59:20,131 --> 00:59:22,767
I may put more pressure on you.

1436
00:59:22,767 --> 00:59:24,736
I thought...

1437
00:59:25,203 --> 00:59:27,372
you would become part of my family.

1438
00:59:31,276 --> 00:59:34,312
I was so happy to see you there yesterday.

1439
00:59:38,550 --> 00:59:41,586
I don't want you to feel pressured.

1440
00:59:41,586 --> 00:59:44,756
Until the very end,

1441
00:59:44,756 --> 00:59:46,124
I'll be cheering for you, Da Hye.

1442
00:59:46,124 --> 00:59:47,292
Thank you so much.

1443
00:59:47,292 --> 00:59:49,494
I'm sorry I cried so much.

1444
00:59:49,494 --> 00:59:50,795
Don't be sorry.

1445
00:59:50,795 --> 00:59:53,364
Can I keep hoping...

1446
00:59:53,364 --> 00:59:55,800
for the two of you until the end?

1447
00:59:59,304 --> 01:00:00,839
Da Hye can't bring herself to answer.

1448
01:00:00,839 --> 01:00:02,040
Goodness.

1449
01:00:02,740 --> 01:00:04,909
I shouldn't be so selfish.

1450
01:00:05,877 --> 01:00:07,745
I'm not trying to pressure you.

1451
01:00:07,745 --> 01:00:09,380
But for me, it's always been you.

1452
01:00:10,882 --> 01:00:13,518
Think carefully tonight.

1453
01:00:13,518 --> 01:00:15,220
I'll be rooting for you to the end.

1454
01:00:18,022 --> 01:00:21,359
Even after I shared how I felt,

1455
01:00:21,726 --> 01:00:24,229
she kept repeating...

1456
01:00:25,029 --> 01:00:28,700
that she'd still support Shin Woo and me.

1457
01:00:30,301 --> 01:00:31,469
Today of all days,

1458
01:00:31,469 --> 01:00:33,905
with the final choice tomorrow,

1459
01:00:34,806 --> 01:00:38,843
that added even more pressure...

1460
01:00:38,843 --> 01:00:42,380
and made the weight on me feel heavier.

1461
01:00:44,315 --> 01:00:49,888
(Da Hye breaks down after she leaves.)

1462
01:01:02,700 --> 01:01:03,768
No.

1463
01:01:07,772 --> 01:01:08,673
What's wrong?

1464
01:01:14,012 --> 01:01:15,880
Who asked to meet you?

1465
01:01:15,880 --> 01:01:17,615
- Shin Woo's mother?
- Yes.

1466
01:01:17,615 --> 01:01:18,516
What did she say?

1467
01:01:21,519 --> 01:01:24,789
Did my actions...

1468
01:01:24,789 --> 01:01:26,624
make Shin Woo think I was sure of him?

1469
01:01:28,259 --> 01:01:30,061
Did I really act that way?

1470
01:01:32,897 --> 01:01:36,167
Did she say you made him feel certain?

1471
01:01:36,835 --> 01:01:38,203
No.

1472
01:01:38,203 --> 01:01:40,405
I'm just looking back to see if I did.

1473
01:01:43,575 --> 01:01:46,044
But she didn't actually say that?

1474
01:01:50,481 --> 01:01:53,518
Her wording and tone...

1475
01:01:53,518 --> 01:01:57,422
felt so pushy and overwhelming.

1476
01:01:57,422 --> 01:01:59,858
Even though I clearly told her...

1477
01:01:59,858 --> 01:02:02,193
that I felt pressured,

1478
01:02:02,193 --> 01:02:04,662
she kept putting more on me.

1479
01:02:05,730 --> 01:02:07,232
It all feels so heavy.

1480
01:02:08,766 --> 01:02:10,602
Still, thanks to Shin Woo,

1481
01:02:10,602 --> 01:02:13,404
I got to pick a good room.

1482
01:02:13,404 --> 01:02:16,508
I didn't get zero votes the first time,

1483
01:02:16,508 --> 01:02:19,177
all thanks to him.

1484
01:02:19,177 --> 01:02:20,812
I was really grateful for all of that.

1485
01:02:21,679 --> 01:02:23,081
That's human nature.

1486
01:02:23,081 --> 01:02:26,351
When you're grateful,

1487
01:02:26,351 --> 01:02:27,685
you talk and see if it can grow into more.

1488
01:02:27,685 --> 01:02:28,620
Right.

1489
01:02:28,620 --> 01:02:31,222
You spend time together...

1490
01:02:32,790 --> 01:02:34,392
to see if it might become something.

1491
01:02:34,392 --> 01:02:37,395
That's what I thought we were doing.

1492
01:02:37,395 --> 01:02:39,364
But I don't know if he mistook that...

1493
01:02:39,364 --> 01:02:42,333
for me "falling in love."

1494
01:02:43,034 --> 01:02:44,636
Now I'm looking back...

1495
01:02:44,636 --> 01:02:46,070
and wondering if I acted...

1496
01:02:46,070 --> 01:02:47,805
like my feelings ran that deep.

1497
01:02:48,306 --> 01:02:51,843
- She never did.
- Not to that degree.

1498
01:02:51,843 --> 01:02:53,545
But she just let things play out.

1499
01:02:54,345 --> 01:02:59,184
She let him go on believing it...

1500
01:02:59,184 --> 01:03:02,220
and left room for misunderstanding.

1501
01:03:04,355 --> 01:03:06,191
She brought me gifts.

1502
01:03:06,191 --> 01:03:07,659
As she explained each gift,

1503
01:03:07,659 --> 01:03:12,163
she said they were all very precious.

1504
01:03:12,864 --> 01:03:15,667
But instead of feeling grateful,

1505
01:03:16,267 --> 01:03:19,504
I felt she hadn't considered me at all.

1506
01:03:20,238 --> 01:03:23,241
I kept thinking Ye Chan's mother
would never have spoken to me that way.

1507
01:03:23,241 --> 01:03:25,476
I'm sorry to say that.

1508
01:03:25,944 --> 01:03:28,980
I found myself comparing the two mothers.

1509
01:03:29,914 --> 01:03:31,516
I'm not sure about that.

1510
01:03:31,516 --> 01:03:34,686
Making that comparison out of nowhere...

1511
01:03:34,686 --> 01:03:36,988
and saying all of that...

1512
01:03:36,988 --> 01:03:39,257
felt like going too far.

1513
01:03:39,257 --> 01:03:41,292
I don't think that's fair.

1514
01:03:41,292 --> 01:03:44,562
Shin Woo's mother...

1515
01:03:44,562 --> 01:03:46,631
felt sorry for her son and came out...

1516
01:03:46,631 --> 01:03:50,401
to plead his case.

1517
01:03:50,401 --> 01:03:53,204
She also did her very best...

1518
01:03:53,204 --> 01:03:55,673
for her son until the end.

1519
01:03:56,608 --> 01:03:58,376
- You're back.
- Yes.

1520
01:03:58,376 --> 01:03:59,611
Did your talk go well, Mom?

1521
01:03:59,611 --> 01:04:00,411
Yes.

1522
01:04:01,279 --> 01:04:03,348
(Glances over)

1523
01:04:03,348 --> 01:04:05,350
Why? Did something happen?

1524
01:04:06,317 --> 01:04:07,252
What is it?

1525
01:04:08,520 --> 01:04:09,621
Did you cry?

1526
01:04:09,621 --> 01:04:11,256
No, Da Hye did.

1527
01:04:11,256 --> 01:04:12,223
Why did she cry?

1528
01:04:13,191 --> 01:04:14,225
What's the problem?

1529
01:04:14,225 --> 01:04:16,027
I told her I liked her.

1530
01:04:16,394 --> 01:04:18,897
But she said she couldn't give us
what I was hoping for.

1531
01:04:18,897 --> 01:04:19,998
I see.

1532
01:04:19,998 --> 01:04:22,967
I told her my choices were clear.

1533
01:04:22,967 --> 01:04:25,637
I said she was my first and second choice.

1534
01:04:25,637 --> 01:04:27,906
I told her I felt the same yesterday too.

1535
01:04:27,906 --> 01:04:30,675
But what worries me is your father...

1536
01:04:30,675 --> 01:04:35,280
brought up religion without meaning to.

1537
01:04:36,114 --> 01:04:38,983
I said religion didn't matter,

1538
01:04:38,983 --> 01:04:42,587
and that I hoped for a good outcome.

1539
01:04:42,587 --> 01:04:45,089
I told her to think it over tonight.

1540
01:04:45,456 --> 01:04:47,959
Then she cried and said she was sorry.

1541
01:04:48,560 --> 01:04:50,061
So tomorrow,

1542
01:04:52,430 --> 01:04:54,833
she may decide not to choose you.

1543
01:04:56,000 --> 01:04:58,570
I asked if I could still hold out hope.

1544
01:04:58,570 --> 01:05:00,972
- I kept asking until the end.
- Good.

1545
01:05:00,972 --> 01:05:02,340
On Match to Marry: With Parents 2,

1546
01:05:02,340 --> 01:05:05,743
we're looking for singles who want
to find a partner with their parents.

1547
01:05:05,743 --> 01:05:06,945
Those who do, please apply now.

1548
01:05:07,745 --> 01:05:09,147
(The final interviews continue.)

1549
01:05:09,147 --> 01:05:10,815
I don't think I have anything else to add.

1550
01:05:10,815 --> 01:05:12,050
I just wanted to see you.

1551
01:05:12,050 --> 01:05:13,251
Thank you.

1552
01:05:13,251 --> 01:05:15,320
Whether I'll make a final choice,

1553
01:05:15,320 --> 01:05:16,588
I don't know yet.

1554
01:05:16,588 --> 01:05:18,990
It's the last day,
and they're saying that?

1555
01:05:18,990 --> 01:05:20,325
Have you pretty much decided?

1556
01:05:21,459 --> 01:05:23,061
Things may end up going the other way.

1557
01:05:23,061 --> 01:05:25,730
There's someone I'm drawn to too.

1558
01:05:25,730 --> 01:05:27,499
I think that's when I got confused.

1559
01:05:27,499 --> 01:05:29,601
The final choice will now begin.

1560
01:05:29,601 --> 01:05:31,169
For my final choice...

1561
01:05:31,169 --> 01:05:32,270
My final choice is...

1562
01:05:32,403 --> 01:05:34,439
(Twist after twist)

1563
01:05:34,439 --> 01:05:36,140
(An unexpected choice)

1564
01:05:36,140 --> 01:05:37,876
This is exciting.

1565
01:05:37,876 --> 01:05:39,677
- They're thinking very hard.
- They are.

1566
01:05:39,677 --> 01:05:41,179
(The final hurdle,
whether the mothers approve or reject)

1567
01:05:41,179 --> 01:05:42,747
Goodness, really?

1568
01:05:42,747 --> 01:05:44,048
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
